WEBVTT

1
00:01:33,583 --> 00:01:35,833
We're the only two survivors
from our company.

2
00:01:38,625 --> 00:01:39,666
We have won,

3
00:01:40,916 --> 00:01:42,416
but this is the price of war.

4
00:01:44,208 --> 00:01:46,458
They paid a far greater price than we did.

5
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:50,583
We killed more than
1,000 Pakistani soldiers.

6
00:01:52,291 --> 00:01:53,375
It's not about them.

7
00:01:55,041 --> 00:01:56,500
{\an8}It's about our soldiers.

8
00:01:57,583 --> 00:01:59,083
That's why I'm here.

9
00:02:02,208 --> 00:02:04,125
This was neither the first war
nor the last.

10
00:02:06,083 --> 00:02:09,208
But the wars to come
will not end like this.

11
00:02:19,791 --> 00:02:21,125
A secret program.

12
00:02:24,208 --> 00:02:27,333
To prepare the next generation
of Indian soldiers.

13
00:02:28,708 --> 00:02:32,541
{\an8}Soldiers who will rewrite the rules
of warfare.

14
00:02:35,458 --> 00:02:37,375
I have the trial permission.

15
00:02:39,875 --> 00:02:42,583
But to make sure the program stays
permanent, I need you.

16
00:02:43,916 --> 00:02:44,958
{\an8}Why me?

17
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:49,375
Because you know
the price of war, Guru <i>ji.</i>

18
00:03:18,791 --> 00:03:20,583
{\an8}India's most important offshore oilfield,

19
00:03:21,791 --> 00:03:22,791
Mumbai High,

20
00:03:24,166 --> 00:03:25,375
is in great danger.

21
00:03:32,166 --> 00:03:35,125
<i>Terrorists have attacked Mumbai High</i>
<i>via a sea route.</i>

22
00:03:35,708 --> 00:03:37,958
<i>Twenty-eight ONGC workers are being</i>
<i>held hostage.</i>

23
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:41,791
<i>If we try to save them,</i>

24
00:03:42,166 --> 00:03:45,500
<i>they've threatened to blow up</i>
<i>the oil rig.</i>

25
00:03:46,375 --> 00:03:49,208
The terrorists have the hostages
and the first-mover advantage.

26
00:03:49,750 --> 00:03:50,958
How will you defeat them?

27
00:03:51,583 --> 00:03:52,541
Come in, Charlie One.

28
00:03:53,208 --> 00:03:55,083
This is Colonel Fateh Singh Lakhawat.

29
00:03:56,541 --> 00:03:58,125
<i>Team, proceed to target.</i>

30
00:03:58,208 --> 00:04:01,250
Risking such an important mission
with a new team?

31
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:03,791
Not a risk. Guts.

32
00:04:05,625 --> 00:04:06,583
No guts…

33
00:04:07,958 --> 00:04:08,958
no glory.

34
00:04:11,083 --> 00:04:14,250
How can they breathe without
oxygen cylinders?

35
00:04:14,333 --> 00:04:17,833
{\an8}My soldiers can hold their breath
underwater for seven to nine minutes

36
00:04:18,291 --> 00:04:20,208
<i>without reducing their swimming speed.</i>

37
00:04:28,666 --> 00:04:30,666
<i>Alpha One. Fourteen targets in all, sir.</i>

38
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:33,583
Seven on deck, four in the control room,

39
00:04:33,666 --> 00:04:35,750
and three on the lower level
with the hostages.

40
00:04:36,166 --> 00:04:39,916
They aren't wearing night vision glasses.
How can they still see?

41
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:41,250
Dr. Cherian,

42
00:04:41,791 --> 00:04:43,625
they don't need to see

43
00:04:43,708 --> 00:04:45,083
because they can hear.

44
00:04:47,291 --> 00:04:50,416
<i>Their hearing ability beats</i>
<i>that of an ordinary person.</i>

45
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:54,416
Come in, Charlie One. It's a go!

46
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:55,375
Go.

47
00:04:55,833 --> 00:04:56,750
One shot.

48
00:04:58,625 --> 00:04:59,541
One kill.

49
00:05:02,541 --> 00:05:03,458
{\an8}No luck.

50
00:05:06,333 --> 00:05:07,250
{\an8}All skill.

51
00:05:17,708 --> 00:05:18,583
Bomb defused.

52
00:05:19,708 --> 00:05:20,875
Hostages released, sir.

53
00:05:20,958 --> 00:05:22,333
Move! To the exit!

54
00:05:22,541 --> 00:05:24,708
<i>Team terrorists, you lost!</i>
<i>Get up!</i>

55
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:27,666
<i>Chin up, guys. Chin up!</i>

56
00:05:27,750 --> 00:05:29,375
<i>- Great job, guys.</i>
<i>- Well done, boys.</i>

57
00:05:33,375 --> 00:05:35,500
That was a war games exercise!

58
00:05:35,916 --> 00:05:39,083
Ladies and gentlemen,
presenting Team Alpha.

59
00:05:39,166 --> 00:05:41,333
The first. The fastest.

60
00:05:41,708 --> 00:05:42,666
The strongest.

61
00:05:43,708 --> 00:05:45,666
<i>Reflexes matching an eagle.</i>

62
00:05:47,541 --> 00:05:49,583
<i>Strength to floor wrestlers.</i>

63
00:05:51,083 --> 00:05:54,083
<i>They've run in</i>
<i>minus 30-degree temperatures,</i>

64
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:56,166
<i>where most people struggle to breathe.</i>

65
00:05:56,250 --> 00:05:58,958
<i>India's most elite and advanced</i>
<i>commando program.</i>

66
00:05:59,041 --> 00:06:02,750
Human lethal weapons, with Alpha
running through their veins.

67
00:06:02,833 --> 00:06:05,416
{\an8}- Alpha?
- Yes, Alpha.

68
00:06:06,291 --> 00:06:08,625
{\an8}The team was injected with the serum,

69
00:06:09,333 --> 00:06:11,416
{\an8}then they were trained by our very best.

70
00:06:11,791 --> 00:06:13,958
Lt. Col. Vikrant Kaul.

71
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:16,458
{\an8}My Guru <i>ji.</i>

72
00:06:19,041 --> 00:06:21,000
I lost an eye in the Kargil attack,

73
00:06:21,708 --> 00:06:24,625
{\an8}but my vision is sharper than ever.

74
00:06:24,958 --> 00:06:27,458
I trained Cobra, Ghatak
and many other teams,

75
00:06:27,708 --> 00:06:31,791
but I've never seen an attack team
like Alpha.

76
00:06:32,208 --> 00:06:33,375
{\an8}They're bloody good.

77
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,291
And that's an understatement.

78
00:06:36,833 --> 00:06:41,041
{\an8}But according to protocol,
you should've taken clearance from DRDO.

79
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:44,833
Do you know the meaning
of top secret, madam?

80
00:06:48,125 --> 00:06:49,750
"Strictly need-to-know basis."

81
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:52,041
Understand what science means,
Col. Lakhawat?

82
00:06:52,125 --> 00:06:53,750
Or do you ignore it, too?

83
00:06:53,833 --> 00:06:55,708
You're the one who ignored it, madam.

84
00:06:56,291 --> 00:06:58,083
{\an8}You didn't look carefully.

85
00:06:59,458 --> 00:07:02,875
The Chief Scientist in this program
is your senior

86
00:07:03,083 --> 00:07:05,000
in experience and qualification.

87
00:07:06,166 --> 00:07:07,541
Doctor John Verghese.

88
00:07:09,291 --> 00:07:10,250
Hello, everyone.

89
00:07:15,833 --> 00:07:16,791
The Alpha serum.

90
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:22,208
It makes our tissues, muscles, and organs
stronger and more efficient.

91
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:26,833
It improves vision, hearing,
reflexes, senses, and lungs.

92
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:29,708
Improves everything.

93
00:07:31,041 --> 00:07:33,541
{\an8}What if a soldier is hit by a bullet?

94
00:07:35,041 --> 00:07:37,666
Soldiers are not invincible.
They're human.

95
00:07:38,375 --> 00:07:41,666
A headshot would kill them.

96
00:07:41,750 --> 00:07:45,666
But if the wound isn't serious,
the Alpha serum can heal it.

97
00:07:46,791 --> 00:07:51,583
In nature, many creatures like lizards
and lobsters can regenerate.

98
00:07:52,208 --> 00:07:56,583
The Alpha serum acts on damaged organs
by mimicking that process.

99
00:07:57,208 --> 00:08:00,125
The initial idea was to facilitate…

100
00:08:01,583 --> 00:08:03,500
faster recovery for our soldiers.

101
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,000
How often must this serum be administered?
Before every mission?

102
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:09,500
Once you go Alpha,

103
00:08:10,291 --> 00:08:11,541
you can't go back.

104
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,916
We need everyone's approval to
take this program to the next level.

105
00:08:32,458 --> 00:08:34,458
{\an8}Did you talk to Janaki's sister?

106
00:08:34,708 --> 00:08:37,083
She was going to get a second opinion
in Spain.

107
00:08:37,708 --> 00:08:39,250
Yes, I received Aruna's email.

108
00:08:39,458 --> 00:08:40,916
I'm glad we found out in time.

109
00:08:41,041 --> 00:08:42,000
Found out what?

110
00:08:42,958 --> 00:08:46,375
I'm a bloody scientist, Preeti.
I don't believe in luck.

111
00:08:46,791 --> 00:08:49,416
Not in sugar-coating either.
Just give me the facts, please.

112
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:50,958
It's confirmed.

113
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:53,916
Congenital heart disease.

114
00:08:57,291 --> 00:09:00,000
During pregnancy, the mother's heart
has to work double.

115
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:03,166
Your heart can't handle it.

116
00:09:04,291 --> 00:09:06,166
This is suicidal, Janaki.

117
00:09:06,375 --> 00:09:08,708
It's your first trimester.
It's still possible.

118
00:09:09,458 --> 00:09:10,500
You need to have an abortion.

119
00:09:12,750 --> 00:09:14,833
So I can never be a mother?

120
00:09:26,583 --> 00:09:28,166
We don't have a choice, Janaki.

121
00:09:29,375 --> 00:09:30,250
Please.

122
00:09:31,750 --> 00:09:32,958
I'm with you.

123
00:09:33,583 --> 00:09:34,958
We'll face it together.

124
00:09:35,333 --> 00:09:37,000
We've tried for so many years.

125
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:39,041
It's too much of a risk.

126
00:09:39,666 --> 00:09:42,041
If I feared death,
I would not have married a soldier.

127
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:46,333
I listened to my heart then,
and I'll listen to it now.

128
00:09:49,083 --> 00:09:50,041
My heart is weak,

129
00:09:53,041 --> 00:09:54,541
but it has made a decision.

130
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,333
Why are you so stubborn?

131
00:09:58,625 --> 00:10:00,875
Stubborn girls change the world, Vikrant.

132
00:10:02,833 --> 00:10:04,958
This child has chosen us.

133
00:10:07,708 --> 00:10:09,208
We're having this baby.

134
00:10:10,666 --> 00:10:11,583
Promise me?

135
00:10:20,041 --> 00:10:21,833
<i>Your heart can't handle it.</i>

136
00:10:22,583 --> 00:10:26,166
<i>My heart is weak,</i>
<i>but it has made a decision.</i>

137
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:30,583
<i>It makes our tissues, muscles, and organs</i>
<i>stronger and more efficient.</i>

138
00:10:31,916 --> 00:10:34,708
{\an8}<i>The Alpha serum repairs</i>
<i>damaged organs.</i>

139
00:10:37,166 --> 00:10:38,625
{\an8}<i>We're having this baby.</i>

140
00:10:41,833 --> 00:10:42,833
{\an8}<i>Promise me?</i>

141
00:10:50,125 --> 00:10:51,458
This is a medical miracle.

142
00:10:52,208 --> 00:10:53,750
Janaki's heart is improving.

143
00:10:53,958 --> 00:10:57,083
It's showing rapid improvement.
And no complications with the pregnancy.

144
00:10:58,208 --> 00:11:00,208
Janaki, it's the last two months.

145
00:11:00,416 --> 00:11:01,375
So take care, okay?

146
00:11:02,833 --> 00:11:03,750
Thank you.

147
00:11:09,375 --> 00:11:10,291
Come.

148
00:11:19,416 --> 00:11:20,958
Our Alpha soldiers.

149
00:11:24,333 --> 00:11:25,291
Brain hemorrhage.

150
00:11:26,583 --> 00:11:29,291
Three of the six died on the spot
from a brain bleed.

151
00:11:30,666 --> 00:11:32,291
The other three are in the ICU.

152
00:11:33,375 --> 00:11:35,958
According to the program,
my team has been

153
00:11:36,708 --> 00:11:39,708
monitoring their vitals for the past
ten months. Every day.

154
00:11:41,125 --> 00:11:44,125
Their vitals were perfect.
There was no warning.

155
00:11:45,041 --> 00:11:47,958
- Sir, you know why this happened, right?
- Alpha.

156
00:11:57,833 --> 00:11:58,750
Move!

157
00:12:22,833 --> 00:12:24,833
<i>We're trying to save the child.</i>

158
00:12:29,458 --> 00:12:30,500
Guru <i>ji.</i>

159
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:33,166
Did you give the Alpha serum to Janaki?

160
00:12:39,041 --> 00:12:42,500
{\an8}I thought I would save her.

161
00:12:42,583 --> 00:12:45,916
{\an8}You didn't save her. You killed her!

162
00:12:48,791 --> 00:12:51,625
{\an8}Alpha is the property
of the Indian Government.

163
00:12:52,291 --> 00:12:56,125
It was only tried on soldiers,
who signed up for it.

164
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:57,875
{\an8}Do you understand what this means?

165
00:13:01,041 --> 00:13:04,791
{\an8}The Alpha serum is running
through your child's veins.

166
00:13:05,875 --> 00:13:08,041
Your baby belongs to the country.

167
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:11,291
{\an8}Only the country has rights
over the child, not you.

168
00:13:16,541 --> 00:13:17,416
Vikrant.

169
00:13:20,291 --> 00:13:21,166
I'm sorry.

170
00:13:21,666 --> 00:13:23,166
We couldn't save Janaki.

171
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:37,291
Take the baby away.

172
00:13:50,250 --> 00:13:51,208
Vikrant!

173
00:13:52,458 --> 00:13:53,625
Vikrant! Listen to me.

174
00:13:55,375 --> 00:13:56,791
They've taken your daughter.

175
00:14:07,291 --> 00:14:08,250
Where's my daughter?

176
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:16,541
She's gone numb.

177
00:14:17,125 --> 00:14:18,208
She's cold.

178
00:14:20,333 --> 00:14:21,791
She's not breathing, Fateh.

179
00:14:22,208 --> 00:14:23,333
She's dead, Guru <i>ji.</i>

180
00:14:29,416 --> 00:14:30,916
You shouldn't have stolen the serum.

181
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,625
{\an8}But I won't let them arrest you.

182
00:14:34,208 --> 00:14:36,416
I respect soldiers like you.

183
00:14:40,666 --> 00:14:41,625
{\an8}I was a soldier.

184
00:14:44,083 --> 00:14:44,958
{\an8}I'm done.

185
00:15:03,750 --> 00:15:05,958
Internal Inquiry has testified that

186
00:15:06,166 --> 00:15:09,875
Alpha should have been tested
for another six months.

187
00:15:09,958 --> 00:15:11,125
But you pushed it.

188
00:15:11,583 --> 00:15:12,791
I did.

189
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:16,625
Nor did I ask for anyone's permission.

190
00:15:16,916 --> 00:15:18,583
Six cadets are dead.

191
00:15:18,916 --> 00:15:21,000
If this version of Alpha had worked,

192
00:15:21,875 --> 00:15:23,666
how many cadets would've been saved?

193
00:15:24,375 --> 00:15:28,375
What use is blood
if it does not spill for the nation?

194
00:15:28,916 --> 00:15:32,708
A bullet didn't kill them.
Your negligence did.

195
00:15:33,041 --> 00:15:35,958
Disobeying orders is not a mistake.
It's a crime.

196
00:15:36,041 --> 00:15:39,458
Under normal circumstances,
the punishment is court-martial.

197
00:15:39,541 --> 00:15:42,541
But considering your exemplary
career record,

198
00:15:42,625 --> 00:15:46,208
this Committee has decided to take
disciplinary action instead.

199
00:15:46,666 --> 00:15:47,666
We're demoting you.

200
00:15:48,625 --> 00:15:51,333
<i>You'll be demoted from Colonel</i>
<i>to Lt. Colonel.</i>

201
00:15:53,333 --> 00:15:57,166
<i>You're now posted to the Cherrapunji</i>
<i>Special Forces base.</i>

202
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:02,208
<i>A place where you'll never see</i>
<i>the battlefield again.</i>

203
00:16:08,708 --> 00:16:10,083
And as for the Alpha program,

204
00:16:10,791 --> 00:16:13,041
it has been shut down permanently.

205
00:16:17,083 --> 00:16:18,916
Despite this humiliation

206
00:16:19,875 --> 00:16:21,833
and this injustice,

207
00:16:23,458 --> 00:16:24,958
one thing has not changed.

208
00:16:26,333 --> 00:16:27,875
That I am a patriot.

209
00:16:29,166 --> 00:16:30,666
A true patriot.

210
00:16:32,666 --> 00:16:34,083
Mark my words.

211
00:16:35,291 --> 00:16:36,875
The day will come

212
00:16:38,875 --> 00:16:41,791
when you'll hold up my patriotism
as an example to the world.

213
00:16:45,041 --> 00:16:46,791
You have no idea that

214
00:16:48,125 --> 00:16:51,500
by shutting down Alpha today,

215
00:16:52,708 --> 00:16:55,333
what a grave mistake you've made.

216
00:16:58,250 --> 00:16:59,250
Not a mistake.

217
00:17:01,166 --> 00:17:02,125
A sin.

218
00:17:07,166 --> 00:17:08,166
<i>Jai Hind!</i>

219
00:17:35,250 --> 00:17:37,083
I need money and men.

220
00:17:37,833 --> 00:17:38,791
When can we meet?

221
00:18:09,875 --> 00:18:11,625
<i>Sir, I'm in Rajasthan,</i>

222
00:18:12,333 --> 00:18:14,416
and you're far away in Cherrapunji.

223
00:18:15,083 --> 00:18:17,083
How can we work together?

224
00:18:17,416 --> 00:18:21,500
I've been posted to such
an inconsequential place

225
00:18:22,333 --> 00:18:24,250
where no one watches me.

226
00:18:24,750 --> 00:18:26,333
Even though I'm posted in Cherrapunji,

227
00:18:26,916 --> 00:18:28,750
my full focus will be on our program.

228
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:33,750
Look! Alpha's new facility.

229
00:18:34,291 --> 00:18:36,166
But how?

230
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,041
There are some people

231
00:18:39,250 --> 00:18:41,666
who understand the importance of Alpha.

232
00:18:42,250 --> 00:18:43,208
Who are they, sir?

233
00:18:43,708 --> 00:18:45,916
A few patriots like me.

234
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:47,708
This was their factory.

235
00:18:48,416 --> 00:18:49,875
Put all your focus on Alpha.

236
00:18:51,291 --> 00:18:52,708
Create a version of the serum

237
00:18:53,416 --> 00:18:56,375
that can be given to every Indian soldier.

238
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,833
Sir, you never give up, do you?

239
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Why would I?

240
00:19:01,458 --> 00:19:04,583
Especially now that
I hold the ace in the pack.

241
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:15,125
Sir, giving Col. Kaul a stillborn baby
that belonged to someone else

242
00:19:15,208 --> 00:19:18,166
and telling him it was his daughter
was wrong.

243
00:19:18,833 --> 00:19:21,958
Sometimes the line between
right and wrong is blurred, Verghese.

244
00:19:22,708 --> 00:19:26,041
And for me,
nothing matters more than Alpha.

245
00:19:30,916 --> 00:19:32,416
What should we call her, sir?

246
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,041
Her mother's name was Janaki.

247
00:19:37,083 --> 00:19:38,208
We'll call her…

248
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:41,875
Sita.

249
00:20:03,375 --> 00:20:06,791
{\an8}The baby elephant is with his family,
who protects him.

250
00:20:06,875 --> 00:20:08,166
{\an8}And my parents?

251
00:20:09,666 --> 00:20:10,583
{\an8}Where are they?

252
00:20:11,958 --> 00:20:13,166
{\an8}They abandoned you.

253
00:20:14,416 --> 00:20:15,916
{\an8}Fateh sir brought you here.

254
00:20:28,916 --> 00:20:29,958
{\an8}Verghese Uncle!

255
00:20:31,250 --> 00:20:33,458
<i>Verghese, is the effect</i>
<i>of Alpha showing?</i>

256
00:20:34,166 --> 00:20:35,250
{\an8}<i>Not yet, sir.</i>

257
00:20:50,083 --> 00:20:51,708
{\an8}Happy 12th birthday, Sita!

258
00:20:51,958 --> 00:20:53,583
Uncle, didn't Fateh sir come?

259
00:20:54,166 --> 00:20:56,958
He's very busy.
Otherwise, he'd be here.

260
00:20:58,208 --> 00:20:59,708
Wait. One minute.

261
00:21:01,875 --> 00:21:03,416
{\an8}This is your birthday gift.

262
00:21:04,416 --> 00:21:05,291
{\an8}Wow!

263
00:21:06,958 --> 00:21:07,875
Soldier!

264
00:21:20,375 --> 00:21:22,666
{\an8}<i>Coding and hacking.</i>
<i>She's excellent at both, sir.</i>

265
00:21:23,708 --> 00:21:25,541
{\an8}Way beyond her age.

266
00:21:26,166 --> 00:21:27,625
{\an8}Her IQ is very high, sir.

267
00:21:27,708 --> 00:21:29,291
{\an8}We don't need her to write a book.

268
00:21:30,333 --> 00:21:32,333
{\an8}Tell me, has Alpha shown its effect?

269
00:22:07,875 --> 00:22:09,500
<i>It's the puberty hormone.</i>

270
00:22:10,125 --> 00:22:11,625
{\an8}Alpha has finally kicked in.

271
00:22:12,416 --> 00:22:14,958
{\an8}Through Sita, we'll be able
to develop a new version of Alpha.

272
00:22:29,833 --> 00:22:31,750
{\an8}Are you crying? I see tears.

273
00:22:32,208 --> 00:22:33,125
{\an8}Don't cry.

274
00:22:33,666 --> 00:22:37,916
{\an8}People are either strong or weak.
Gender has nothing to do with it.

275
00:22:39,416 --> 00:22:41,958
{\an8}<i>There are two kinds of people</i>
<i>in this world.</i>

276
00:22:42,250 --> 00:22:43,958
{\an8}<i>Wolves and sheep.</i>

277
00:22:44,416 --> 00:22:45,375
{\an8}I'm a wolf.

278
00:22:46,875 --> 00:22:47,750
{\an8}What are you?

279
00:22:47,875 --> 00:22:49,416
{\an8}A wolf's child is a wolf, sir.

280
00:22:55,291 --> 00:22:56,208
{\an8}<i>Well done!</i>

281
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:57,666
{\an8}Here's your reward.

282
00:23:00,208 --> 00:23:02,250
{\an8}What did you call your father?

283
00:23:02,333 --> 00:23:03,208
{\an8}Baba.

284
00:23:04,291 --> 00:23:05,166
{\an8}Baba.

285
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,916
I got it for my first mission.

286
00:23:10,583 --> 00:23:12,458
{\an8}When will I get my first mission?

287
00:23:13,416 --> 00:23:15,458
{\an8}When you become an Indian soldier.

288
00:23:21,625 --> 00:23:22,666
What's this?

289
00:23:23,833 --> 00:23:24,708
Alpha.

290
00:23:25,666 --> 00:23:26,708
What's Alpha?

291
00:23:26,958 --> 00:23:29,125
The first letter of the Greek alphabet,

292
00:23:29,583 --> 00:23:31,291
and our program's motto.

293
00:23:32,166 --> 00:23:33,333
The first.

294
00:23:33,500 --> 00:23:34,791
The fastest.

295
00:23:35,208 --> 00:23:36,333
The strongest.

296
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:40,291
If you look closely, every city
is an urban jungle,

297
00:23:41,125 --> 00:23:43,791
and in that jungle, Alpha rules.

298
00:23:43,875 --> 00:23:48,458
That's why I called the serum "Alpha."
And that's what you are.

299
00:23:49,375 --> 00:23:50,250
Alpha.

300
00:24:20,333 --> 00:24:21,250
{\an8}Sir!

301
00:24:21,333 --> 00:24:24,000
{\an8}Sir, it's Tel Aviv. The Mossad Chief
wants a word.

302
00:24:24,083 --> 00:24:26,833
{\an8}- Cancel everything. This takes priority.
- Yes, sir.

303
00:24:26,916 --> 00:24:27,791
Let's get to it.

304
00:24:28,083 --> 00:24:29,250
- Karan.
- Yes, sir.

305
00:24:29,333 --> 00:24:30,666
- Show me.
- Sir.

306
00:24:32,208 --> 00:24:33,416
Sir, five bodies were found.

307
00:24:33,833 --> 00:24:35,666
The first was Subrato Das.

308
00:24:36,291 --> 00:24:37,666
<i>He was traveling alone</i>
<i>in the last metro.</i>

309
00:24:40,416 --> 00:24:42,083
<i>Just one stab. Dead.</i>

310
00:24:43,416 --> 00:24:45,458
<i>Five hours later, Amit Thakur.</i>

311
00:24:46,250 --> 00:24:48,166
{\an8}<i>He saw someone ahead,</i>
<i>so he honked.</i>

312
00:24:49,958 --> 00:24:50,958
<i>The car was rigged.</i>

313
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,875
Number three, Ajinkya Sethi.
A sniper kill, sir.

314
00:24:55,166 --> 00:24:58,750
The bullet went through the window and
his glasses, straight into his left eye.

315
00:25:00,791 --> 00:25:02,166
Next was Madhur Kulkarni.

316
00:25:03,458 --> 00:25:04,666
<i>In broad daylight, a headshot.</i>

317
00:25:05,708 --> 00:25:06,708
<i>Fearless.</i>

318
00:25:09,166 --> 00:25:12,625
The last and most ruthless, Susan Cherian.

319
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:19,833
<i>Suffocated to death.</i>

320
00:25:22,625 --> 00:25:24,791
Sir, they've all been murdered
in the past 48 hours.

321
00:25:25,041 --> 00:25:27,333
All from different departments
and ministries.

322
00:25:27,583 --> 00:25:29,416
DRDO, NSA, NSG,

323
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:31,833
Military Intelligence,
and the Ministry of Defense.

324
00:25:31,916 --> 00:25:36,000
We're trying to work out the common link
that made them targets.

325
00:25:44,666 --> 00:25:45,583
Alpha.

326
00:25:58,625 --> 00:26:01,541
ID Sita. 14:25 hours.

327
00:26:02,291 --> 00:26:03,250
Access granted.

328
00:26:31,875 --> 00:26:32,916
Where were you for the last two days?

329
00:26:35,500 --> 00:26:36,500
What are you eating?

330
00:26:39,875 --> 00:26:40,791
Thanks.

331
00:26:41,541 --> 00:26:42,500
I haven't had breakfast.

332
00:26:46,833 --> 00:26:47,750
So…

333
00:27:09,958 --> 00:27:11,583
Sita, what are you doing?

334
00:27:28,625 --> 00:27:29,666
Good morning, Baba.

335
00:27:31,250 --> 00:27:33,875
{\an8}Today Sita herself has come
to burn Lanka.

336
00:27:47,583 --> 00:27:48,625
<i>Sita has gone crazy!</i>

337
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:50,708
<i>She's killing everyone. Find her.</i>

338
00:27:54,666 --> 00:27:56,916
<i>Let's get her! Get the bombs!</i>
<i>Get the guns!</i>

339
00:28:09,750 --> 00:28:10,708
Grenade!

340
00:28:33,166 --> 00:28:34,041
Hi, boys.

341
00:29:30,375 --> 00:29:32,166
<i>Where are my parents?</i>

342
00:29:39,333 --> 00:29:40,791
<i>Happy 12th birthday, Sita!</i>

343
00:29:40,875 --> 00:29:42,583
<i>- Uncle, didn't Fateh sir come?</i>
<i>- He's very busy.</i>

344
00:29:44,333 --> 00:29:46,083
<i>I'm a wolf. What are you?</i>

345
00:29:46,416 --> 00:29:47,416
<i>One shot.</i>

346
00:29:47,875 --> 00:29:48,750
<i>One kill!</i>

347
00:29:49,500 --> 00:29:50,750
<i>There's only one punishment</i>
<i>for a traitor.</i>

348
00:29:50,833 --> 00:29:52,291
<i>There's only one punishment</i>
<i>for a traitor.</i>

349
00:29:52,541 --> 00:29:54,083
<i>On your 18th birthday,</i>

350
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:56,291
<i>what could be more special than that?</i>

351
00:29:57,041 --> 00:29:58,041
<i>One kill!</i>

352
00:31:54,625 --> 00:31:56,583
<i>Target in sight! Target in sight!</i>

353
00:31:56,708 --> 00:31:57,875
<i>Sita is on the bridge.</i>

354
00:31:58,000 --> 00:32:01,041
<i>Don't lose visual. I repeat.</i>
<i>Do not lose the visual.</i>

355
00:32:01,541 --> 00:32:02,708
<i>No one will shoot!</i>

356
00:32:05,375 --> 00:32:06,625
Have you lost it?

357
00:32:07,041 --> 00:32:08,083
Hands up, Sita!

358
00:32:08,625 --> 00:32:09,791
Drop the gun!

359
00:32:11,333 --> 00:32:12,375
Put the gun down!

360
00:34:23,208 --> 00:34:28,541
Why did RandAW Chief Vikrant Kaul travel
to a remote corner of the country

361
00:34:28,875 --> 00:34:30,541
to meet a forgotten soldier?

362
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,083
I had no choice.

363
00:34:37,833 --> 00:34:42,041
Honestly, Guru <i>ji,</i> stay out of this.
It's in your best interest.

364
00:34:42,458 --> 00:34:43,583
What are you up to, Fateh?

365
00:35:06,875 --> 00:35:07,875
{\an8}<i>I've killed six.</i>

366
00:35:08,750 --> 00:35:09,666
{\an8}<i>Now just two left.</i>

367
00:35:16,958 --> 00:35:17,875
Who is she?

368
00:35:18,208 --> 00:35:19,166
How did you get this?

369
00:35:22,291 --> 00:35:25,833
Look carefully. You know her.

370
00:35:26,166 --> 00:35:27,750
She's very close to you.

371
00:35:39,833 --> 00:35:41,916
I buried my daughter
with my own two hands.

372
00:35:43,125 --> 00:35:44,125
Sita.

373
00:35:45,708 --> 00:35:47,208
Her name is Sita.

374
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:00,875
Sita became the Alpha soldier
we all hoped for.

375
00:36:01,500 --> 00:36:04,291
She was my pride. Our very best.

376
00:36:04,958 --> 00:36:06,583
Then one day she flipped.

377
00:36:07,041 --> 00:36:08,875
The serum twisted her brain.

378
00:36:09,458 --> 00:36:11,416
Everyone associated with the program…

379
00:36:12,541 --> 00:36:13,916
she's killing them all.

380
00:36:14,541 --> 00:36:17,500
Special Forces shut Alpha down
twenty years ago.

381
00:36:18,541 --> 00:36:19,791
How are you running it?

382
00:36:20,708 --> 00:36:22,875
Who is funding it?

383
00:36:25,625 --> 00:36:27,333
I never thought you'd become a traitor!

384
00:36:27,833 --> 00:36:29,791
Sita is the traitor, Guru <i>ji.</i>

385
00:36:30,208 --> 00:36:32,125
She's killing our national assets.

386
00:36:32,208 --> 00:36:35,541
Now she's after the RandAW Chief
and a Lt. Colonel.

387
00:36:36,208 --> 00:36:37,375
Don't worry.

388
00:36:37,666 --> 00:36:39,041
My men are looking for her.

389
00:36:39,458 --> 00:36:41,750
When they find her, they'll kill her.

390
00:36:41,833 --> 00:36:43,041
She's my daughter, Fateh.

391
00:36:43,416 --> 00:36:46,291
How? You don't even know her.

392
00:36:47,041 --> 00:36:51,375
You can't imagine how hard
it is for me to kill her.

393
00:36:52,583 --> 00:36:55,041
Your daughter died twenty years ago.

394
00:36:55,791 --> 00:36:57,333
Now she's my Sita.

395
00:36:59,708 --> 00:37:01,791
I'll expose the truth
about you to everyone,

396
00:37:02,458 --> 00:37:03,833
and you'll hang for it.

397
00:37:05,708 --> 00:37:06,666
I will.

398
00:37:09,166 --> 00:37:10,625
But only after Sita.

399
00:37:11,625 --> 00:37:14,041
After all, she's the one murdering people.

400
00:37:14,708 --> 00:37:17,708
Don't let your emotions cloud
your judgment again, Guru <i>ji.</i>

401
00:37:18,791 --> 00:37:20,583
The last time you did that,

402
00:37:21,666 --> 00:37:23,000
you lost your wife.

403
00:37:24,166 --> 00:37:25,833
This time it may be your daughter.

404
00:37:55,791 --> 00:37:56,833
I hate coffee.

405
00:37:58,166 --> 00:38:00,041
Baba gave me the habit, Soldier.

406
00:38:00,375 --> 00:38:02,041
One cup for him,

407
00:38:03,125 --> 00:38:04,041
and one for me.

408
00:38:05,041 --> 00:38:06,708
I'll have my last cup with him.

409
00:38:10,583 --> 00:38:12,250
I'll get our revenge, Soldier.

410
00:38:13,208 --> 00:38:14,750
Two lab rats have survived.

411
00:38:15,083 --> 00:38:16,791
But we'll kill Baba at the very end.

412
00:38:17,416 --> 00:38:19,000
Like enjoying a fine dessert
after lunch.

413
00:38:23,041 --> 00:38:24,500
We'll save the best for the last.

414
00:38:26,625 --> 00:38:29,291
But before that… Vikrant Kaul.

415
00:38:31,750 --> 00:38:34,000
Kaul. A Kashmiri Pandit surname.

416
00:38:34,208 --> 00:38:36,250
Sanskrit for "family."

417
00:38:37,625 --> 00:38:40,416
He left the army 20 years ago.
Then he went totally off the grid.

418
00:38:40,500 --> 00:38:43,875
After Luthra died, he was
suddenly appointed RandAW Chief.

419
00:38:44,291 --> 00:38:46,208
Congratulations, Vikrant!

420
00:38:51,666 --> 00:38:52,583
I love it.

421
00:39:01,083 --> 00:39:02,125
Okay.

422
00:39:02,583 --> 00:39:06,250
Two weeks ago, he flew from Delhi
to Madrid, from there to Valladolid.

423
00:39:06,791 --> 00:39:09,708
Four days later, he came back to India
from Spain.

424
00:39:09,791 --> 00:39:14,208
The same route last month.
In March too. And in December.

425
00:39:15,708 --> 00:39:17,416
These RandAW guys love travelling!

426
00:39:18,166 --> 00:39:19,416
He's in Spain again?

427
00:39:20,875 --> 00:39:21,791
Sad.

428
00:39:23,166 --> 00:39:25,166
We'll have to wait
till he's back in India.

429
00:39:33,250 --> 00:39:35,666
Soldier, all his trips to Spain
were on commercial flights.

430
00:39:36,791 --> 00:39:38,125
That means personal trips.

431
00:39:41,750 --> 00:39:43,625
What's special about Spain, Kaul?

432
00:40:11,416 --> 00:40:13,333
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

433
00:40:14,083 --> 00:40:16,166
<i>A firecracker</i>

434
00:40:16,500 --> 00:40:17,625
<i>No touching</i>

435
00:40:18,625 --> 00:40:20,875
<i>Lightning striking</i>

436
00:40:20,958 --> 00:40:22,333
<i>Girl's a storm</i>

437
00:40:23,333 --> 00:40:25,333
<i>Challenge her</i>

438
00:40:25,666 --> 00:40:26,958
<i>You've had it</i>

439
00:40:27,791 --> 00:40:29,875
<i>Acts first</i>

440
00:40:30,125 --> 00:40:31,458
<i>Thinks later</i>

441
00:40:32,750 --> 00:40:34,833
<i>Kohl-lined eyes</i>

442
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:37,083
<i>Burning through the heart</i>

443
00:40:37,291 --> 00:40:40,541
<i>Encircles the heart</i>
<i>Now she's gone</i>

444
00:40:40,791 --> 00:40:42,958
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

445
00:40:43,041 --> 00:40:45,250
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

446
00:40:45,333 --> 00:40:47,791
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

447
00:40:47,916 --> 00:40:49,875
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

448
00:40:49,958 --> 00:40:52,041
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

449
00:40:52,125 --> 00:40:54,333
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

450
00:40:54,500 --> 00:40:56,833
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

451
00:40:56,916 --> 00:40:58,958
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

452
00:40:59,916 --> 00:41:01,958
<i>Soft breeze</i>

453
00:41:02,166 --> 00:41:04,375
<i>Wind perplexed</i>

454
00:41:04,500 --> 00:41:06,500
<i>Sturdy form</i>

455
00:41:06,750 --> 00:41:07,875
<i>Kickass</i>

456
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:09,000
<i>Kickass</i>

457
00:41:09,083 --> 00:41:11,041
<i>Challenge her</i>

458
00:41:11,333 --> 00:41:12,500
<i>You've had it</i>

459
00:41:12,583 --> 00:41:13,541
<i>You've had it</i>

460
00:41:13,666 --> 00:41:15,541
<i>Acts first</i>

461
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:17,041
<i>Thinks later</i>

462
00:41:40,625 --> 00:41:42,750
<i>Those eyes of hers</i>

463
00:41:42,833 --> 00:41:45,208
<i>Robs the whole village</i>

464
00:41:45,416 --> 00:41:47,583
<i>She heeds no one</i>

465
00:41:47,666 --> 00:41:49,375
<i>Her law is law</i>

466
00:41:49,458 --> 00:41:51,583
<i>Sweet as honey</i>

467
00:41:51,666 --> 00:41:53,833
<i>Melting in the mouth</i>

468
00:41:53,916 --> 00:41:56,750
<i>Showers colors</i>

469
00:41:56,833 --> 00:41:58,541
<i>To the world</i>

470
00:41:58,625 --> 00:42:00,583
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

471
00:42:00,666 --> 00:42:02,916
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

472
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:05,583
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

