<i>Girl's a storm</i>

482
00:42:26,916 --> 00:42:28,750
<i>Challenge her</i>

483
00:42:29,041 --> 00:42:30,333
<i>You've had it</i>

484
00:42:30,500 --> 00:42:33,208
<i>- Cast off the evil eye</i>
<i>- Acts first</i>

485
00:42:33,291 --> 00:42:35,000
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

486
00:43:06,041 --> 00:43:07,041
<i>Vikrant, listen to me.</i>

487
00:43:08,750 --> 00:43:10,208
{\an8}They've taken your daughter.

488
00:43:10,875 --> 00:43:13,041
{\an8}No, listen! I want to show you something.

489
00:43:13,375 --> 00:43:14,916
{\an8}Just come. Just come with me.

490
00:43:15,333 --> 00:43:17,166
I overheard Colonel Fateh.

491
00:43:17,416 --> 00:43:21,041
{\an8}The Alpha serum is running
through your child's veins.

492
00:43:21,625 --> 00:43:23,708
Your baby belongs to the country.

493
00:43:25,083 --> 00:43:26,208
Your other daughter.

494
00:43:28,375 --> 00:43:30,583
- What?
- I'm sorry, Vikrant.

495
00:43:30,833 --> 00:43:34,333
{\an8}Janaki knew, but she didn't tell you.
She also stopped me from telling you.

496
00:43:36,041 --> 00:43:37,458
Having one baby was a risk,

497
00:43:38,208 --> 00:43:41,291
and she knew you'd never let her
carry two babies.

498
00:43:42,541 --> 00:43:45,166
They're twins, but not identical.

499
00:43:46,041 --> 00:43:48,333
The sister, who was born first,
protected the other.

500
00:43:49,916 --> 00:43:53,333
No one must know about this.
And please--

501
00:43:53,416 --> 00:43:54,708
I'll delete all the records.

502
00:43:59,958 --> 00:44:02,458
<i>Thanks, Aruna, for bringing her here.</i>

503
00:44:02,875 --> 00:44:05,250
Vikrant, how will you live without her?

504
00:44:06,416 --> 00:44:07,708
She's our niece.

505
00:44:08,416 --> 00:44:09,958
We'll be more than happy
to have her, but…

506
00:44:10,625 --> 00:44:11,666
you're her father.

507
00:44:12,291 --> 00:44:14,208
I have no option, Manish.

508
00:44:14,916 --> 00:44:16,791
No one must know she's my daughter.

509
00:44:18,625 --> 00:44:20,250
I want her to lead a normal life.

510
00:44:20,416 --> 00:44:23,208
When she's older and starts
asking questions…

511
00:44:24,208 --> 00:44:25,250
I'll tell her the truth

512
00:44:27,458 --> 00:44:29,458
about what happened
to her mother and sister.

513
00:44:32,333 --> 00:44:33,916
Thought of a name for her?

514
00:44:34,500 --> 00:44:35,791
You know Janaki loved this name…

515
00:44:37,750 --> 00:44:38,708
Durga.

516
00:44:40,500 --> 00:44:43,666
The destroyer of demons. Durga.

517
00:44:45,500 --> 00:44:47,541
I always said you were special.

518
00:44:48,041 --> 00:44:49,541
There was no one like you.

519
00:44:50,583 --> 00:44:51,583
But there is someone, Durga.

520
00:44:52,458 --> 00:44:53,583
She's just like you.

521
00:44:57,833 --> 00:45:00,833
<i>This is Mom, this is you,</i>
<i>and this is my sister.</i>

522
00:45:01,041 --> 00:45:02,500
<i>And I'm the one behind her.</i>

523
00:45:02,958 --> 00:45:04,791
<i>She always protected me.</i>

524
00:45:05,375 --> 00:45:07,750
Pa, did you think of a name for her?

525
00:45:16,250 --> 00:45:17,291
Si…

526
00:45:18,791 --> 00:45:19,791
Sita?

527
00:45:22,166 --> 00:45:24,083
- Is she okay?
- She's in terrible danger.

528
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:28,541
Fateh will kill her.

529
00:45:30,166 --> 00:45:31,208
Or she'll kill Fateh.

530
00:45:33,500 --> 00:45:34,500
And you too.

531
00:45:35,625 --> 00:45:37,708
To be honest, she should kill me.

532
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:39,708
Because I've been
a horrible father to her.

533
00:45:39,791 --> 00:45:41,375
What? No, no, no.
Pa, listen to me.

534
00:45:42,000 --> 00:45:43,458
You're the best father in the world.

535
00:45:44,583 --> 00:45:46,791
When you got the chance,
you did your best.

536
00:45:48,041 --> 00:45:49,625
What happened was not your fault.

537
00:45:52,500 --> 00:45:53,583
I need your help.

538
00:45:55,958 --> 00:45:57,166
We need to find her.

539
00:45:57,791 --> 00:45:59,833
We have to save her at any cost.

540
00:46:02,291 --> 00:46:03,458
If Sita is caught,

541
00:46:04,583 --> 00:46:06,875
she'll be arrested for the murders.

542
00:46:07,500 --> 00:46:09,916
As the RandAW Chief,
I can't protect her officially.

543
00:46:11,291 --> 00:46:12,666
We have to do it unofficially.

544
00:46:13,541 --> 00:46:15,416
Only you and me.

545
00:46:16,041 --> 00:46:18,833
For Sita. For our family.

546
00:46:19,375 --> 00:46:21,416
Maybe I trained you for this day.

547
00:46:27,708 --> 00:46:33,000
Pa, not a day has gone by that
I haven't missed my sister, Sita.

548
00:46:34,833 --> 00:46:37,333
She was born first
so she could protect me.

549
00:46:38,333 --> 00:46:41,000
I've always wondered
how I'd ever repay her.

550
00:46:43,708 --> 00:46:45,250
I guess this is my only chance.

551
00:46:47,500 --> 00:46:49,000
Let's bring Sita home, Pa.

552
00:46:51,250 --> 00:46:53,041
Let's make our family a family again.

553
00:47:01,250 --> 00:47:02,291
We got him, Soldier!

554
00:47:05,291 --> 00:47:08,083
Yes! Mr. Family Man
is coming back to India.

555
00:47:08,458 --> 00:47:12,291
Spain Air 5837A. Madrid to Delhi,
Delhi to Srinagar.

556
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:14,750
Srinagar? Kashmir?

557
00:47:15,458 --> 00:47:16,458
Why Kashmir?

558
00:47:23,958 --> 00:47:24,958
Come on, Sita!

559
00:47:25,833 --> 00:47:28,166
He's Kashmiri. Of course
he'd have a home in Kashmir.

560
00:47:28,625 --> 00:47:31,791
Vikrant Kaul,
property registrations? Nothing.

561
00:47:36,791 --> 00:47:37,833
<i>Any other family member?</i>

562
00:47:37,916 --> 00:47:39,458
<i>Janaki Kaul. Wife.</i>

563
00:47:43,791 --> 00:47:44,666
Boom!

564
00:47:48,541 --> 00:47:49,791
Nicely done, Janaki.

565
00:47:50,458 --> 00:47:52,083
Such a huge house in Betaab Valley!

566
00:48:16,083 --> 00:48:17,000
Cool.

567
00:48:37,541 --> 00:48:38,416
Pretty.

568
00:49:07,166 --> 00:49:08,500
Was it necessary to travel separately?

569
00:49:08,791 --> 00:49:10,666
<i>It's for your own safety, kiddo.</i>

570
00:49:10,958 --> 00:49:12,833
Being careful is the new brave.

571
00:49:13,958 --> 00:49:16,375
That's quite cool. Just like this house.

572
00:49:18,750 --> 00:49:21,750
Wow, Pa! Ma had some great taste.

573
00:49:21,875 --> 00:49:23,708
This is so beautiful!

574
00:49:24,166 --> 00:49:27,375
This place has been my off-grid
personal base for years.

575
00:49:27,458 --> 00:49:29,083
<i>It's my own safe house.</i>

576
00:49:29,541 --> 00:49:31,875
The kitchen is completely stocked up.

577
00:49:32,125 --> 00:49:34,083
Your favorite Italian coffee
is there too.

578
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:35,875
Coffee.

579
00:49:36,041 --> 00:49:37,333
I'll get there ASAP.

580
00:49:37,458 --> 00:49:38,541
<i>Okay. See you, Pa.</i>

581
00:49:38,750 --> 00:49:39,958
- Love you.
- Love you.

582
00:50:19,333 --> 00:50:20,208
Cool.

583
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:47,083
Sita?

584
00:51:48,208 --> 00:51:49,916
Fateh sent you for me?

585
00:51:53,000 --> 00:51:54,083
He has hurt my ego.

586
00:51:55,375 --> 00:51:57,708
No, no, no. I'm so sorry.
I didn't know.

587
00:51:57,916 --> 00:51:59,250
I'm your sister.

588
00:52:01,666 --> 00:52:02,583
Sister?

589
00:52:04,000 --> 00:52:04,958
Should I tie you a <i>rakhi?</i>

590
00:52:25,250 --> 00:52:26,208
Sita.

591
00:52:28,375 --> 00:52:31,208
I just want to talk to you. Please.

592
00:52:31,791 --> 00:52:32,791
The rule is simple.

593
00:52:33,333 --> 00:52:35,875
If you can stop me, then you get to talk.

594
00:52:46,916 --> 00:52:47,916
Can we talk now?

595
00:53:05,250 --> 00:53:06,250
Still wanna talk?

596
00:54:21,625 --> 00:54:22,958
So you wanna sit and talk?

597
00:54:24,208 --> 00:54:25,125
Okay.

598
00:54:27,583 --> 00:54:28,875
You shouldn't have laughed.

599
00:55:01,958 --> 00:55:04,708
Sita… that's our father.

600
00:55:23,041 --> 00:55:23,958
Sita.

601
00:55:25,875 --> 00:55:26,833
Papa.

602
00:55:36,583 --> 00:55:37,458
Pa!

603
00:55:46,875 --> 00:55:47,958
We don't look alike.

604
00:56:13,416 --> 00:56:14,291
Want some?

605
00:56:15,333 --> 00:56:16,625
You've gotten plenty of cardio too.

606
00:56:17,916 --> 00:56:18,791
Don't eat.

607
00:56:19,083 --> 00:56:20,875
I'm just loving this <i>desi </i>Chinese.

608
00:56:22,916 --> 00:56:23,791
I…

609
00:56:24,458 --> 00:56:25,708
I'm so sorry, kiddo.

610
00:56:29,208 --> 00:56:30,125
"Kiddo"?

611
00:56:32,125 --> 00:56:33,458
Don't get ahead of yourself, Kaul.

612
00:56:34,666 --> 00:56:35,583
And you?

613
00:56:35,875 --> 00:56:36,916
What nonsense were you saying?

614
00:56:38,166 --> 00:56:40,666
That we're sisters?
And he's our father?

615
00:56:41,166 --> 00:56:42,166
That's the truth.

616
00:56:42,416 --> 00:56:43,291
Shut up!

617
00:56:47,583 --> 00:56:48,458
Who is she?

618
00:56:50,291 --> 00:56:51,166
My mother?

619
00:56:51,541 --> 00:56:53,500
Yes. Janaki.

620
00:56:54,458 --> 00:56:56,416
- Didn't she come on the family vacation?
- She died…

621
00:56:57,250 --> 00:56:58,750
after giving birth to you both.

622
00:57:03,000 --> 00:57:03,875
Sita…

623
00:57:06,375 --> 00:57:09,208
you and I are twins.
I'm exactly like you.

624
00:57:11,208 --> 00:57:12,708
Look, sis, you're good.

625
00:57:13,125 --> 00:57:14,750
It's been a while since
anyone challenged me.

626
00:57:16,916 --> 00:57:18,333
But exactly like me?

627
00:57:27,875 --> 00:57:29,083
Who are these two boring people?

628
00:57:29,708 --> 00:57:30,625
My parents.

629
00:57:31,333 --> 00:57:32,875
I mean, my adoptive parents.

630
00:57:35,708 --> 00:57:38,000
Adoptive parents?

631
00:57:46,250 --> 00:57:47,666
How many parents does she have?

632
00:57:47,791 --> 00:57:48,708
Listen to me--

633
00:57:56,958 --> 00:58:00,083
She has three parents here
and one in heaven.

634
00:58:01,375 --> 00:58:02,541
And what did I get?

635
00:58:04,583 --> 00:58:05,458
Fateh.

636
00:58:07,958 --> 00:58:09,833
What's the difference between
a guinea pig and me?

637
00:58:13,083 --> 00:58:17,333
What is the difference between
a guinea pig and me, Kaul?

638
00:58:22,041 --> 00:58:25,041
After a few days of experiments,
the guinea pig

639
00:58:25,125 --> 00:58:27,541
is put down using sodium pentobarbital.

640
00:58:29,958 --> 00:58:32,541
And me? I didn't even get that option.

641
00:58:38,833 --> 00:58:41,291
Sita, Fateh lied to Pa.

642
00:58:41,916 --> 00:58:43,833
Pa thought you were dead all this time.

643
00:58:45,083 --> 00:58:46,416
If I'd known about you,

644
00:58:46,708 --> 00:58:49,708
none of this would've happened.
I'd have come to save you.

645
00:58:49,791 --> 00:58:50,750
Like you've come today?

646
00:59:01,083 --> 00:59:02,000
What is it, sis?

647
00:59:03,458 --> 00:59:04,541
Feeling bad for me?

648
00:59:16,208 --> 00:59:17,708
Honestly, I feel bad for you.

649
00:59:18,083 --> 00:59:19,166
What's this circus?

650
00:59:19,750 --> 00:59:20,750
What's going on here?

651
00:59:21,958 --> 00:59:22,833
Birthday.

652
00:59:22,916 --> 00:59:24,375
- Which one?
- Eighteenth.

653
00:59:28,000 --> 00:59:29,041
Eighteenth birthday?

654
00:59:31,250 --> 00:59:32,666
Same day, right?

655
00:59:35,833 --> 00:59:38,166
I wish I had a photo
from my 18th birthday.

656
00:59:39,000 --> 00:59:40,708
Quite the party it was!

657
00:59:44,958 --> 00:59:46,958
Happy 18th birthday, Sita.

658
00:59:47,333 --> 00:59:48,333
Thank you, Baba.

659
00:59:49,958 --> 00:59:53,625
Thank you for the dress
and for the dinner.

660
00:59:54,000 --> 00:59:55,125
Thank you for everything.

661
00:59:55,708 --> 00:59:56,958
It really means a lot to me.

662
01:00:13,916 --> 01:00:14,833
Wazeer.

663
01:00:15,083 --> 01:00:16,083
Arms dealer.

664
01:00:18,666 --> 01:00:20,791
He's a bloody traitor.

665
01:00:23,458 --> 01:00:24,541
Kill him.

666
01:00:25,250 --> 01:00:28,916
And then you'll see what
a soldier's life is all about.

667
01:00:32,791 --> 01:00:34,458
So all this wasn't for my birthday?

668
01:00:35,875 --> 01:00:37,500
On your 18th birthday,

669
01:00:37,750 --> 01:00:40,375
you're going to undertake your
first mission for the country.

670
01:00:41,500 --> 01:00:43,625
What could be more special than that?

671
01:01:16,000 --> 01:01:18,250
Take off your clothes and come.

672
01:01:18,625 --> 01:01:19,541
Join the party.

673
01:01:55,458 --> 01:01:56,416
Happy birthday!

674
01:02:02,208 --> 01:02:03,333
That was the first time.

675
01:02:05,416 --> 01:02:06,416
My first kill.

676
01:02:08,916 --> 01:02:12,333
After that, Fateh kept giving me targets,
and I kept killing them.

677
01:02:14,583 --> 01:02:17,916
Fateh got his Alpha soldier,
and I got my life's purpose.

678
01:02:20,750 --> 01:02:22,750
Then one day, everything changed.

679
01:02:25,875 --> 01:02:28,333
Next target. John Verghese.

680
01:02:33,875 --> 01:02:36,333
Stay sharp, or you're dead.

681
01:02:39,875 --> 01:02:42,666
Baba, how can I kill Dr. Verghese?

682
01:02:43,083 --> 01:02:44,291
Verghese is a traitor.

683
01:02:45,041 --> 01:02:46,958
He betrayed the country.

684
01:02:47,750 --> 01:02:50,291
And there's only one punishment
for a traitor.

685
01:03:01,958 --> 01:03:04,458
There's only one punishment for a traitor.

686
01:03:06,000 --> 01:03:06,875
Death.

687
01:03:06,958 --> 01:03:08,625
There's only one punishment for a traitor!

688
01:03:09,416 --> 01:03:10,291
Death.

689
01:03:15,666 --> 01:03:18,541
<i>For me, Baba's words were always</i>
<i>set in stone.</i>

690
01:03:19,416 --> 01:03:20,291
Yes.

691
01:03:28,416 --> 01:03:29,541
<i>But for the first time,</i>

692
01:03:30,291 --> 01:03:31,333
<i>I couldn't shoot.</i>

693
01:03:31,875 --> 01:03:33,541
I was waiting for you, Sita.

694
01:03:38,708 --> 01:03:40,750
Before dying,
I wanted to tell you something.

695
01:03:43,125 --> 01:03:47,458
And then Uncle Verghese told me
the story of my life.

696
01:03:50,500 --> 01:03:51,458
And Alpha's.

697
01:03:52,166 --> 01:03:53,666
<i>Have you ever thought about Alpha?</i>

698
01:03:54,583 --> 01:03:56,916
<i>Why aren't there more soldiers like you?</i>

699
01:03:59,166 --> 01:04:01,708
Because everyone who was given
the Alpha serum has died,

700
01:04:02,458 --> 01:04:03,500
except you.

701
01:04:06,208 --> 01:04:07,958
Fateh has only one purpose in life.

702
01:04:08,708 --> 01:04:11,916
To find out how more soldiers
like you could be created.

703
01:04:12,708 --> 01:04:15,916
You might remember that I collected
your blood samples every week

704
01:04:16,541 --> 01:04:19,541
to try and understand how you were
the only survivor.

705
01:04:19,791 --> 01:04:21,333
Why the serum hadn't killed you,

706
01:04:22,416 --> 01:04:25,708
and whether I could make a new version
of Alpha from your blood?

707
01:04:26,708 --> 01:04:29,041
But we didn't have cadets to test it on.

708
01:04:29,333 --> 01:04:32,583
So, Fateh had to find new subjects.

709
01:04:35,000 --> 01:04:40,000
Ordinary, innocent people
became the new test subjects…

710
01:04:42,375 --> 01:04:43,541
<i>but none of the poor souls survived.</i>

711
01:04:47,666 --> 01:04:49,541
Then we found this old graveyard.

712
01:04:52,666 --> 01:04:56,208
Fateh filled every grave here.

713
01:05:00,041 --> 01:05:05,208
And he's ready to fill one last grave…

714
01:05:07,833 --> 01:05:09,416
but I can't let that happen.

715
01:05:10,458 --> 01:05:11,458
What do you mean?

716
01:05:12,833 --> 01:05:18,000
The new version of Alpha
will not fail, Sita.

717
01:05:25,041 --> 01:05:26,125
What are you hiding?

718
01:05:28,416 --> 01:05:29,500
A few days ago,

719
01:05:29,791 --> 01:05:33,666
<i>Fateh found my research</i>
<i>on the new version of Alpha.</i>

720
01:05:33,916 --> 01:05:35,541
Verghese, you turned out to be weak.

721
01:05:36,500 --> 01:05:38,791
{\an8}Spending time with Sita

722
01:05:39,625 --> 01:05:40,791
has made you emotional.

723
01:05:41,541 --> 01:05:43,541
How dare you hide this from me?

724
01:05:44,958 --> 01:05:46,333
We can't do this.

725
01:05:48,166 --> 01:05:51,250
We cannot harvest the serum
from Sita's brain cells.

726
01:05:53,125 --> 01:05:56,416
The poor girl will remain
in a medical coma for life.

727
01:06:02,583 --> 01:06:04,250
<i>She'll become a living corpse.</i>

728
01:06:05,208 --> 01:06:06,625
You can't do this, sir.

729
01:06:07,833 --> 01:06:10,125
Sita will be sentenced
to a living death, sir.

730
01:06:18,708 --> 01:06:19,625
Verghese…

731
01:06:21,458 --> 01:06:23,291
bravery demands sacrifice.

732
01:06:30,458 --> 01:06:31,458
Baba.

733
01:06:38,750 --> 01:06:39,750
Baba.

734
01:06:43,708 --> 01:06:45,583
Fateh is ready to kill me?

735
01:06:51,083 --> 01:06:54,166
He didn't just stop there.

736
01:06:54,875 --> 01:06:58,916
After he found the research,
a man came to meet him.

737
01:07:04,125 --> 01:07:05,375
The new version of Alpha.

738
01:07:08,916 --> 01:07:10,041
Congratulations!

739
01:07:14,125 --> 01:07:16,291
There's no stopping Operation Odyssey now.

740
01:07:21,458 --> 01:07:24,791
<i>I have no idea what Operation Odyssey is.</i>

741
01:07:25,583 --> 01:07:28,250
I was scared.
That's why I ran away from the lab.

742
01:07:28,500 --> 01:07:32,125
I tried to warn a few people
about Fateh's evil plans.

743
01:07:33,166 --> 01:07:35,791
They were the same people who approved

744
01:07:36,625 --> 01:07:38,750
the Alpha program twenty years ago.

745
01:07:57,333 --> 01:07:59,250
Fateh claimed they were all traitors.

746
01:07:59,916 --> 01:08:02,916
They weren't traitors.
The real traitor is Fateh.

747
01:08:03,833 --> 01:08:05,916
Fateh's mission must be stopped, Sita.

748
01:08:06,708 --> 01:08:08,041
He's a threat to you.

749
01:08:08,708 --> 01:08:11,208
The secret behind the Alpha serum
lies within you.

750
01:08:14,833 --> 01:08:15,791
So, my dear…

751
01:08:18,416 --> 01:08:19,416
run away.

752
01:08:20,250 --> 01:08:21,458
Far from the facility.

753
01:08:21,875 --> 01:08:25,083
A new team of doctors and surgeons
is coming for the procedure.

754
01:08:25,875 --> 01:08:27,000
- Don't go there.
- Let them come.

755
01:08:28,375 --> 01:08:33,833
This procedure, the new Alpha program,
can only exist if the facility exists.

756
01:08:35,416 --> 01:08:36,708
If Fateh exists.

757
01:08:46,666 --> 01:08:47,541
Sita.

758
01:08:49,916 --> 01:08:53,875
There's a man in that photo,
RandAW Chief Vikrant Kaul.

759
01:08:55,041 --> 01:08:55,958
Go meet him.

760
01:08:56,458 --> 01:08:57,958
He has a story to tell you.

761
01:09:00,375 --> 01:09:01,333
Uncle, no!

762
01:09:20,916 --> 01:09:22,750
Verghese Uncle wanted me to meet you.

763
01:09:24,000 --> 01:09:25,083
Now I know why.

764
01:09:26,416 --> 01:09:28,125
He believed we'd have
a happy family reunion.

765
01:09:30,583 --> 01:09:32,875
But we only have one thing in common.

766
01:09:34,333 --> 01:09:37,250
Our stupidity.
We fell straight into Fateh's trap.

767
01:09:37,666 --> 01:09:39,458
I came here to talk to you,
not to kill you.

768
01:09:40,750 --> 01:09:41,625
You guys are free to go.

769
01:09:46,000 --> 01:09:46,958
Where are you going?

770
01:09:48,750 --> 01:09:51,041
I'm going for Fateh.
Don't follow me.

771
01:09:51,166 --> 01:09:52,083
No.

772
01:09:53,541 --> 01:09:54,416
You're not.

773
01:09:55,458 --> 01:09:57,625
You two will stay here.
Safe and secure.

774
01:09:59,083 --> 01:10:01,000
I'll deal with him. Durga.

775
01:10:03,625 --> 01:10:04,666
Back off, Kaul.

776
01:10:05,916 --> 01:10:06,916
Don't play the father.

777
01:10:07,708 --> 01:10:10,041
I've tried the family scene with Fateh.

778
01:10:11,041 --> 01:10:12,041
It's not for me.

779
01:10:13,000 --> 01:10:16,416
Before I change my mind
and blow your brains out,

780
01:10:16,708 --> 01:10:17,583
go.

781
01:10:18,125 --> 01:10:19,375
I'm not going anywhere.

782
01:10:21,625 --> 01:10:23,291
I lost my daughter once.

783
01:10:26,041 --> 01:10:27,250
I can't lose her again.

784
01:10:33,083 --> 01:10:34,458
You already have a daughter, Kaul.

785
01:10:35,291 --> 01:10:36,666
You celebrate her birthdays,

786
01:10:37,166 --> 01:10:39,791
you celebrate every silly thing
about her life.

787
01:10:42,458 --> 01:10:43,666
I mean nothing to you.

788
01:10:44,500 --> 01:10:46,291
But if you're still finding it hard,

789
01:10:46,583 --> 01:10:48,666
just believe what you've believed
for all these years.

790
01:10:49,541 --> 01:10:52,916
That this daughter of yours
died at birth.

791
01:10:54,125 --> 01:10:55,041
Okay?

792
01:10:57,083 --> 01:10:57,958
Guys!

793
01:11:09,458 --> 01:11:11,958
Heavy boots. All around us.

794
01:11:16,541 --> 01:11:17,416
They're armed.

795
01:11:18,125 --> 01:11:19,083
Rifles.

796
01:11:24,791 --> 01:11:26,375
Fateh followed me.

797
01:12:01,708 --> 01:12:02,875
Found Sita?

798
01:12:03,291 --> 01:12:05,541
Yes, sir. A bike was found
outside the house.

799
01:12:06,166 --> 01:12:08,833
I confirm that both
Kaul and Sita are inside.

800
01:12:09,000 --> 01:12:10,833
Sita mustn't be harmed.

801
01:12:12,666 --> 01:12:14,166
I want her alive.

802
01:12:16,000 --> 01:12:17,000
And Kaul, sir?

803
01:12:17,416 --> 01:12:19,125
Find Sita, then kill him.

804
01:12:19,791 --> 01:12:20,708
<i>Copy that, sir.</i>

805
01:12:26,541 --> 01:12:28,333
Don't take Fateh lightly, Sita.

806
01:12:29,750 --> 01:12:31,375
He's the lion of his jungle.

807
01:12:34,125 --> 01:12:37,791
Lions only pretend to be ferocious.

808
01:12:39,750 --> 01:12:41,875
It's the lioness who goes for the kill.

809
01:12:43,875 --> 01:12:45,416
And don't forget, my name is Sita!

810
01:12:47,833 --> 01:12:49,583
Let the trial of fire begin!

811
01:13:21,583 --> 01:13:22,750
Sniper, take the shot!

812
01:13:47,333 --> 01:13:48,208
RandAW Chief.

813
01:13:54,208 --> 01:13:56,333
My armory. Come, let's move.

814
01:13:57,708 --> 01:13:59,833
<i>Tools out!</i>
<i>Cutters, pluckers, hammers!</i>

815
01:13:59,916 --> 01:14:01,583
<i>Come on! Break in!</i>

816
01:14:11,041 --> 01:14:11,958
<i>Move in! Move in!</i>

817
01:14:15,541 --> 01:14:16,625
Both of you, leave.

818
01:14:16,958 --> 01:14:19,708
There's a door that leads to the forest.

819
01:14:20,041 --> 01:14:21,208
Come on, girls. Now!

820
01:14:21,416 --> 01:14:23,166
I don't run away
from the battlefield, Kaul.

821
01:14:23,541 --> 01:14:26,833
This is not running.
It's called a strategic retreat.

822
01:14:27,208 --> 01:14:29,500
Sometimes stepping back
is moving forward in war.

823
01:14:29,750 --> 01:14:31,375
And right now, there's a whole army
out there.

824
01:14:31,458 --> 01:14:34,125
How many? Twenty? Thirty?

825
01:14:34,458 --> 01:14:35,833
- Listen…
- It's not your cup of tea…

826
01:14:35,916 --> 01:14:38,250
- Listen to me.
- but this is what Fateh trained me for.

827
01:14:38,333 --> 01:14:39,333
And I trained him!

828
01:14:42,041 --> 01:14:44,708
Sita, I know it's hard,

829
01:14:45,041 --> 01:14:47,625
but right now you have to trust Pa.

830
01:14:50,541 --> 01:14:51,500
How can I trust anyone?

831
01:14:52,625 --> 01:14:54,041
Put yourself in my shoes.

832
01:14:54,625 --> 01:14:56,333
That's what I've done since
I was a kid.

833
01:14:56,958 --> 01:14:58,708
When I found out you were still alive,

834
01:14:58,916 --> 01:15:01,333
I've often wondered what if it was…

835
01:15:03,291 --> 01:15:04,166
me.

836
01:15:04,875 --> 01:15:08,375
If I was born a few seconds
before you on that day,

837
01:15:08,916 --> 01:15:10,750
what would've happened?

838
01:15:13,750 --> 01:15:15,541
I would've been raised in a lab,

839
01:15:16,500 --> 01:15:18,916
and you would have had a normal life
in Spain.

840
01:15:20,208 --> 01:15:21,166
But, Sita,

841
01:15:22,333 --> 01:15:24,333
you protected me.

842
01:15:26,958 --> 01:15:30,708
Please give Pa a chance
to protect you today.

843
01:15:33,958 --> 01:15:35,041
<i>Prepare for entry.</i>

844
01:15:38,416 --> 01:15:41,208
We're running out of time.
Give me 72 hours.

845
01:15:41,416 --> 01:15:42,416
You want Fateh, right?

846
01:15:42,666 --> 01:15:44,541
I'll bring him to you.
I promise you that.

847
01:15:50,750 --> 01:15:51,625
Okay.

848
01:15:55,208 --> 01:15:56,333
This phone has the coordinates

849
01:15:57,208 --> 01:15:58,208
of a safe house.

850
01:15:58,750 --> 01:16:00,458
Avoid highways and check posts.

851
01:16:00,541 --> 01:16:02,250
Any more basic advice?

852
01:16:03,125 --> 01:16:05,375
Yes. The most basic of all.

853
01:16:06,625 --> 01:16:07,708
Take care of each other.

854
01:16:11,041 --> 01:16:12,041
Let's go.

855
01:16:20,333 --> 01:16:21,208
The door?

856
01:17:50,666 --> 01:17:53,291
Sir, Kaul is dead. We've found Sita.

857
01:17:53,958 --> 01:17:55,333
<i>Awaiting your instructions.</i>

858
01:17:56,875 --> 01:17:58,583
I'm coming to Kashmir to see Sita.

859
01:17:59,958 --> 01:18:01,750
I'll send you the location.
Bring her there.

860
01:18:07,916 --> 01:18:08,833
This is Kaul.

861
01:18:09,291 --> 01:18:11,458
I'll need a few more days before
returning to headquarters.

862
01:18:11,916 --> 01:18:13,208
I'm away on a personal matter.

863
01:18:14,333 --> 01:18:15,416
But I've found something.

864
01:18:16,750 --> 01:18:19,541
Only one word. Odyssey.

865
01:18:21,916 --> 01:18:24,583
Get me any intel you have on it
from the last 20 years.

866
01:18:26,125 --> 01:18:28,125
I want it in my inbox within four hours.

867
01:18:44,083 --> 01:18:45,583
Stop staring and sleep.

868
01:18:47,333 --> 01:18:49,166
You need at least six hours of sleep.

869
01:18:49,250 --> 01:18:51,791
Or else, your brain will start producing
excess cortisol.

870
01:18:51,875 --> 01:18:54,750
And then, you'll lose focus
and spoil my mood.

871
01:18:54,833 --> 01:18:56,416
No way! You have insomnia too?

872
01:18:58,166 --> 01:18:59,041
Too?

873
01:19:01,833 --> 01:19:04,833
Look, apart from Alpha, there's nothing
in common between us.

874
01:19:07,166 --> 01:19:09,125
Do you always put on this tough-girl act?

875
01:19:11,541 --> 01:19:13,208
You must feel some emotion.

876
01:19:13,625 --> 01:19:16,041
Like deep inside.

877
01:19:18,541 --> 01:19:21,583
If you only feel good when you're
killing someone,

878
01:19:21,666 --> 01:19:23,791
something deep inside you dies.

879
01:19:26,250 --> 01:19:28,416
This tough-girl act isn't an act.

880
01:19:30,083 --> 01:19:31,708
If you were with me,
you would have understood.

881
01:19:37,125 --> 01:19:38,750
I am with you now.

882
01:19:42,291 --> 01:19:44,083
You can trust me, you know.

883
01:19:46,291 --> 01:19:48,958
If I said I trusted you,

884
01:19:50,583 --> 01:19:52,041
would you let me sleep?

885
01:19:52,125 --> 01:19:53,708
Of course! I'll sing you a lullaby too!

886
01:19:55,333 --> 01:19:56,208
Should I?

887
01:19:56,291 --> 01:19:58,708
- Please keep an arm's distance.
- Okay. Easy.

888
01:19:58,875 --> 01:20:00,083
- Breathe in.
- Move back!

889
01:20:00,791 --> 01:20:01,750
Breathe out.

890
01:20:01,875 --> 01:20:04,625
<i>Do you mind takin' me</i>
<i>For a spin around, eh?</i>

891
01:20:04,916 --> 01:20:06,875
<i>Wanna check out if you're in the vibe, eh</i>

892
01:20:06,958 --> 01:20:09,083
<i>She be rollin' like a movie star bae</i>

893
01:20:09,208 --> 01:20:14,416
<i>- We in this together ride or die, eh</i>
<i>- Nothing to fear with you here</i>

894
01:20:14,666 --> 01:20:18,625
<i>With you by my side</i>
<i>I'll stop the storm</i>

895
01:20:18,708 --> 01:20:20,916
<i>Let me have my way</i>

896
01:20:21,083 --> 01:20:23,000
<i>Your way is good too</i>

897
01:20:23,291 --> 01:20:27,708
<i>Let us take a leap of faith</i>

898
01:20:31,333 --> 01:20:35,416
<i>O friend, now I've found you</i>

899
01:20:35,708 --> 01:20:39,666
<i>This world will dance on my fingertips</i>

900
01:20:39,958 --> 01:20:44,000
<i>O friend, for sure</i>

901
01:20:44,250 --> 01:20:48,208
<i>I'll make the sky fall to the ground</i>

902
01:20:48,291 --> 01:20:51,541
<i>Do you mind takin' me</i>
<i>For a spin around, eh?</i>

903
