<i>Do you mind takin' me</i>
<i>For a spin around, eh?</i>

930
01:22:49,916 --> 01:22:52,041
<i>Wanna check out if you're in the vibe, eh</i>

931
01:22:52,166 --> 01:22:54,083
<i>She be rollin' like a movie star bae</i>

932
01:22:54,250 --> 01:22:56,125
<i>We in this together ride or die, eh</i>

933
01:23:25,500 --> 01:23:26,791
Tired of talking non-stop?

934
01:23:28,500 --> 01:23:29,375
Eat!

935
01:23:30,125 --> 01:23:31,583
No more breaks till the safe house.

936
01:23:34,125 --> 01:23:36,833
Kashmiri apple. Pa's favorite.

937
01:23:43,875 --> 01:23:45,083
Listen, don't worry too much.

938
01:23:46,500 --> 01:23:47,541
Kaul is damn tough.

939
01:23:48,458 --> 01:23:49,583
I've read his file.

940
01:23:51,000 --> 01:23:52,041
He can look after himself.

941
01:23:56,208 --> 01:23:57,458
Nothing scares you, right?

942
01:23:58,166 --> 01:24:00,416
Fear affects only those
who have something to lose.

943
01:24:01,916 --> 01:24:03,208
Someone or something you love.

944
01:24:06,125 --> 01:24:07,000
So…

945
01:24:13,208 --> 01:24:14,083
Ma's ring.

946
01:24:16,125 --> 01:24:17,458
You know Ma was a scientist, right?

947
01:24:18,125 --> 01:24:20,458
Like super smart, super headstrong.

948
01:24:20,541 --> 01:24:24,333
Apparently, she could beat Pa
at chess and arm wrestling.

949
01:24:25,791 --> 01:24:27,750
Deadly chick! Just like you.

950
01:24:31,041 --> 01:24:31,958
Keep it.

951
01:24:32,208 --> 01:24:33,708
Now you have something that's yours.

952
01:24:37,458 --> 01:24:38,416
Don't lose it, okay?

953
01:24:41,875 --> 01:24:42,875
No thanks.

954
01:24:44,291 --> 01:24:46,375
- Why did you throw it away?
- Why did you give it to me?

955
01:24:47,291 --> 01:24:48,625
I felt like it.

956
01:24:48,875 --> 01:24:50,791
I thought you'd value it!
It was Ma's!

957
01:24:51,375 --> 01:24:53,166
I thought it'd be important
for both of us.

958
01:24:53,375 --> 01:24:54,250
For you!

959
01:24:55,333 --> 01:24:57,750
Janaki is just a name to me. Okay?

960
01:24:57,833 --> 01:25:00,833
Sita, you were just a name
to me as well, okay?

961
01:25:01,208 --> 01:25:04,625
Stop with this "I don't care,
I'm such a cool bitch" attitude!

962
01:25:04,833 --> 01:25:06,291
Because it's really getting tiring now.

963
01:25:06,750 --> 01:25:08,666
What are you so upset about?

964
01:25:08,750 --> 01:25:10,000
That you grew up without Ma?

965
01:25:10,791 --> 01:25:14,041
Well, guess what?
That's another thing we have in common.

966
01:25:20,208 --> 01:25:23,625
Sometimes, doing things to make
others happy matters the most.

967
01:25:32,208 --> 01:25:34,041
- Bitch!
- Yeah, same to you!

968
01:25:35,250 --> 01:25:36,125
Give me the ring.

969
01:25:40,458 --> 01:25:41,583
Say sorry first.

970
01:25:43,083 --> 01:25:45,333
Don't bore me. Before I change
my mind, just give it.

971
01:26:40,708 --> 01:26:42,541
Hands up! Put the gun down.

972
01:26:49,666 --> 01:26:51,250
<i>RandAW Chief Vikrant Kaul is safe.</i>

973
01:26:52,208 --> 01:26:53,708
<i>Target Fateh Singh Lakhawat in sight.</i>

974
01:26:55,708 --> 01:26:56,750
<i>All clear, over!</i>

975
01:26:59,541 --> 01:27:00,833
Where is Sita?

976
01:27:01,250 --> 01:27:03,625
How could you do this to a child?

977
01:27:03,833 --> 01:27:06,416
She's not a child.
She's a murderer.

978
01:27:11,125 --> 01:27:12,958
You forced her to commit the murders

979
01:27:13,833 --> 01:27:15,416
for Operation Odyssey.

980
01:27:16,500 --> 01:27:18,000
What is Operation Odyssey?

981
01:27:18,791 --> 01:27:20,416
How are you going to use Alpha?

982
01:27:21,166 --> 01:27:24,000
Where is Sita, Guru <i>ji?</i>

983
01:27:26,875 --> 01:27:28,875
You'll start talking
when you're interrogated.

984
01:27:30,541 --> 01:27:31,458
I'm taking you in.

985
01:27:49,916 --> 01:27:51,666
You have no option, Fateh.

986
01:27:53,416 --> 01:27:54,416
I do, Guru <i>ji.</i>

987
01:28:14,416 --> 01:28:15,791
Where is Sita?

988
01:28:42,916 --> 01:28:44,791
This doesn't look like a safe house
from any angle.

989
01:28:48,250 --> 01:28:49,958
Sita? Durga?

990
01:28:51,041 --> 01:28:52,416
He's waiting for you.

991
01:28:52,666 --> 01:28:53,666
"He?"

992
01:28:55,166 --> 01:28:56,458
The Dalai Lama is Kaul's friend?

993
01:29:30,583 --> 01:29:31,583
He's gonna save us?

994
01:29:36,458 --> 01:29:37,875
Namaste! Monk?

995
01:29:38,625 --> 01:29:39,541
What…

996
01:29:40,916 --> 01:29:45,333
Monk <i>ji,</i> our dad, Vikrant Kaul,
sent us to you.

997
01:29:49,458 --> 01:29:50,833
You completed a 75-hour journey

998
01:29:52,208 --> 01:29:53,500
in 66 hours.

999
01:29:54,416 --> 01:29:56,541
Kaul was right. You two are special.

1000
01:29:57,458 --> 01:29:58,333
Come.

1001
01:29:59,041 --> 01:30:00,125
Join me, please.

1002
01:30:00,750 --> 01:30:01,708
Yeah, of course.

1003
01:30:02,000 --> 01:30:02,875
Come.

1004
01:30:10,833 --> 01:30:13,416
Sorry, this is my first time
making a <i>rangoli.</i>

1005
01:30:14,375 --> 01:30:18,250
This is not a<i> rangoli.</i>
It's a mandala.

1006
01:30:19,625 --> 01:30:22,166
In Buddhism, it's considered sacred.

1007
01:30:23,000 --> 01:30:24,375
It's actually so fascinating.

1008
01:30:24,541 --> 01:30:26,833
Sometimes, making a perfect mandala

1009
01:30:27,083 --> 01:30:28,666
takes years.

1010
01:30:29,333 --> 01:30:30,750
Amazing.

1011
01:30:30,833 --> 01:30:32,250
And once it's completed,

1012
01:30:32,708 --> 01:30:36,083
the monks destroy it.

1013
01:30:37,625 --> 01:30:38,916
Then they restart.

1014
01:30:40,750 --> 01:30:42,625
They begin again.

1015
01:30:42,708 --> 01:30:43,708
Okay!

1016
01:30:45,083 --> 01:30:47,583
Did Kaul send us here
for a painting class?

1017
01:30:48,958 --> 01:30:49,875
Let's go.

1018
01:30:51,708 --> 01:30:52,666
Shall we go?

1019
01:30:53,166 --> 01:30:55,875
This sage will get us killed.
Let's go.

1020
01:30:55,958 --> 01:30:56,875
Sita!

1021
01:30:58,208 --> 01:30:59,208
The angry one!

1022
01:31:01,000 --> 01:31:02,875
There was a time when…

1023
01:31:03,958 --> 01:31:05,250
I was dangerous too, just like you.

1024
01:31:06,291 --> 01:31:08,083
In life, there comes a time

1025
01:31:08,541 --> 01:31:13,250
when you must abandon outer noise
for inner peace.

1026
01:31:15,291 --> 01:31:16,333
It's amazing…

1027
01:31:19,041 --> 01:31:20,500
The noise outside is seeping in.

1028
01:31:28,166 --> 01:31:29,291
Don't worry, Monk <i>ji.</i>

1029
01:31:30,583 --> 01:31:32,208
We'll keep you safe. Okay?

1030
01:32:20,875 --> 01:32:21,750
Wanna die?

1031
01:32:22,333 --> 01:32:24,166
No, right? So kill.

1032
01:33:15,750 --> 01:33:18,166
I'll kill him! Stop!

1033
01:33:18,291 --> 01:33:19,916
I'm telling you, I'll kill him!

1034
01:33:25,375 --> 01:33:26,333
Kabir!

1035
01:33:31,000 --> 01:33:31,958
It's Kabir!

1036
01:33:34,875 --> 01:33:35,875
It's Kabir!

1037
01:33:37,375 --> 01:33:38,375
It's Kabir!

1038
01:33:39,000 --> 01:33:40,291
Run! It's Kabir!

1039
01:33:40,916 --> 01:33:42,000
- It's Kabir!
- Run!

1040
01:33:46,791 --> 01:33:47,708
Wait a minute.

1041
01:33:48,208 --> 01:33:50,166
Are you Kabir? The Kabir?

1042
01:33:50,666 --> 01:33:52,291
Who "the Kabir?"

1043
01:33:52,375 --> 01:33:54,000
Pa has told me so much about him.

1044
01:33:54,666 --> 01:33:57,250
This guy's no sage, he's savage!

1045
01:34:06,041 --> 01:34:07,041
Come on, Kabir!

1046
01:34:09,500 --> 01:34:10,583
Time to begin again.

1047
01:36:27,208 --> 01:36:28,083
Durga.

1048
01:36:34,791 --> 01:36:36,791
Alright. You two, back door.

1049
01:36:37,875 --> 01:36:40,500
Khumjung Village. Jethi Amma.
She'll take care of everything.

1050
01:36:41,500 --> 01:36:42,458
Okay.

1051
01:37:15,000 --> 01:37:15,958
Drink it.

1052
01:37:19,125 --> 01:37:20,583
The wound's deep.

1053
01:37:20,833 --> 01:37:23,458
I've given you Kabir's special medicine
for the pain.

1054
01:37:23,750 --> 01:37:26,750
You won't need it after this.

1055
01:37:27,250 --> 01:37:28,958
In twenty minutes, full recovery.

1056
01:37:29,833 --> 01:37:31,250
Now rest.

1057
01:37:33,875 --> 01:37:35,458
- Hello.
<i>- Greetings.</i>

1058
01:37:38,666 --> 01:37:40,083
<i>Don't worry.</i>

1059
01:37:40,583 --> 01:37:41,833
<i>Kaul is alive.</i>

1060
01:37:42,333 --> 01:37:43,458
<i>But for how long?</i>

1061
01:37:43,875 --> 01:37:45,541
That's your decision, Sita.

1062
01:37:46,375 --> 01:37:47,708
Come, save him.

1063
01:37:48,541 --> 01:37:50,583
<i>I haven't seen you for so long.</i>

1064
01:37:52,166 --> 01:37:55,625
Come. I'm dying to meet you, Soldier.

1065
01:38:04,083 --> 01:38:05,041
I'm going.

1066
01:38:05,125 --> 01:38:06,750
Come, let's go. Where to?

1067
01:38:06,875 --> 01:38:09,166
You're not going anywhere.
See the state you're in.

1068
01:38:09,291 --> 01:38:10,416
What do you mean? No way!

1069
01:38:12,125 --> 01:38:13,250
What did Kaul say?

1070
01:38:13,583 --> 01:38:15,666
Sometimes, stepping back
is moving forward.

1071
01:38:17,416 --> 01:38:18,375
You're an Alpha.

1072
01:38:19,291 --> 01:38:21,416
You'll get better soon.
Trust me, you'll be okay.

1073
01:38:30,250 --> 01:38:31,250
You'll be okay, right?

1074
01:38:39,083 --> 01:38:40,125
Sita,

1075
01:38:40,833 --> 01:38:42,583
promise me Pa won't come to any harm.

1076
01:39:38,208 --> 01:39:40,541
- Shit!
- That's a switch mine.

1077
01:39:41,166 --> 01:39:42,041
Don't move.

1078
01:39:57,250 --> 01:39:58,125
Sita…

1079
01:39:59,625 --> 01:40:00,791
throw your gun away.

1080
01:40:05,541 --> 01:40:06,458
{\an8}No.

1081
01:40:38,458 --> 01:40:40,875
She came to avenge her father…

1082
01:40:44,125 --> 01:40:47,041
but her emotions got the better of her,
and she forgot her training.

1083
01:40:49,750 --> 01:40:50,958
I'm your problem.

1084
01:40:51,750 --> 01:40:52,666
And I'm here.

1085
01:40:54,083 --> 01:40:55,041
Let him go.

1086
01:40:55,875 --> 01:40:56,791
Fateh…

1087
01:40:57,458 --> 01:40:59,166
don't you dare touch my daughter!

1088
01:41:00,458 --> 01:41:01,375
What do you want?

1089
01:41:02,208 --> 01:41:03,708
What do I want?

1090
01:41:06,375 --> 01:41:07,250
Alpha.

1091
01:41:09,875 --> 01:41:10,958
Why do I want it?

1092
01:41:11,916 --> 01:41:13,333
What will I do with it?

1093
01:41:14,041 --> 01:41:16,250
You two must have a lot of questions.

1094
01:41:17,083 --> 01:41:18,500
You're so close to me.

1095
01:41:19,500 --> 01:41:20,583
You have every right…

1096
01:41:24,583 --> 01:41:26,125
to know the truth.

1097
01:41:27,833 --> 01:41:29,583
To know the truth about Odyssey.

1098
01:41:32,083 --> 01:41:36,583
{\an8}Guru <i>ji,</i> you used to say I was
the perfect example of a true patriot.

1099
01:41:38,875 --> 01:41:40,208
I still am.

1100
01:41:41,625 --> 01:41:43,791
No one is a greater patriot than I am.

1101
01:41:44,708 --> 01:41:46,166
The only question is…

1102
01:41:51,416 --> 01:41:52,875
a patriot of which country?

1103
01:42:12,250 --> 01:42:13,166
Whose is this?

1104
01:42:13,250 --> 01:42:15,750
The first Pakistani soldier I killed.

1105
01:42:18,500 --> 01:42:23,000
The first Pakistani soldier
you killed was…

1106
01:42:25,375 --> 01:42:26,500
That was me!

1107
01:42:38,458 --> 01:42:40,625
<i>There's a creek between</i>
<i>Karachi and Kutch.</i>

1108
01:42:41,166 --> 01:42:44,666
<i>Because of the high tide,</i>
<i>no one could see the border,</i>

1109
01:42:45,125 --> 01:42:48,083
<i>but I saw a way to enter India.</i>

1110
01:42:48,666 --> 01:42:52,041
<i>26/11 was not the first time</i>
<i>we crossed the waters.</i>

1111
01:42:52,541 --> 01:42:54,791
{\an8}<i>I was the first one.</i>

1112
01:42:54,875 --> 01:42:57,166
{\an8}1989

1113
01:43:09,000 --> 01:43:11,500
<i>ISI ordered me to go to Haryana.</i>

1114
01:43:12,083 --> 01:43:15,041
<i>That was my first strike in India.</i>

1115
01:43:22,375 --> 01:43:23,875
<i>An entire family died,</i>

1116
01:43:24,875 --> 01:43:26,208
<i>except for one boy.</i>

1117
01:43:27,041 --> 01:43:29,541
His name was Fateh Singh Lakhawat.

1118
01:43:36,875 --> 01:43:39,875
<i>I finished him off</i>
<i>and found my new identity.</i>

1119
01:43:51,083 --> 01:43:53,916
I learned to master the local accent.

1120
01:43:58,833 --> 01:44:03,583
I had been fully trained in Pakistan and
met the needs of India's Special Forces.

1121
01:44:04,000 --> 01:44:07,041
{\an8}<i>I was posted in Kashmir.</i>

1122
01:44:12,000 --> 01:44:14,791
<i>And then started the first phase.</i>

1123
01:44:15,541 --> 01:44:17,833
<i>I passed intel to Pakistan through</i>
<i>different ways and methods.</i>

1124
01:44:29,000 --> 01:44:30,708
{\an8}<i>Then came phase two.</i>

1125
01:44:31,208 --> 01:44:33,583
{\an8}<i>Winning the trust of the Special Forces.</i>

1126
01:44:34,291 --> 01:44:36,041
<i>For that, ISI helped</i>
<i>by giving me information</i>

1127
01:44:36,125 --> 01:44:37,958
{\an8}<i>about terrorists operating in India.</i>

1128
01:44:47,125 --> 01:44:49,583
<i>I regretted killing my own people.</i>

1129
01:44:49,666 --> 01:44:52,000
<i>But bravery demands sacrifice.</i>

1130
01:44:56,333 --> 01:44:58,833
{\an8}<i>Thanks to their sacrifice,</i>
<i>I got promoted.</i>

1131
01:44:59,458 --> 01:45:02,833
This is the essence of Operation Odyssey.
Now for its last phase.

1132
01:45:03,375 --> 01:45:07,833
Being a colonel, I had access to
information that I never had before.

1133
01:45:09,083 --> 01:45:11,791
<i>The time had come to attack.</i>

1134
01:45:14,833 --> 01:45:15,708
<i>Guru </i>ji…

1135
01:45:17,125 --> 01:45:18,458
I'm sure you remember

1136
01:45:19,333 --> 01:45:21,000
<i>Poonch, Kupwara,</i>

1137
01:45:21,625 --> 01:45:25,083
<i>and many other places, where we brutally</i>
<i>killed the Special Forces.</i>

1138
01:45:29,916 --> 01:45:33,458
Despite this, we were badly
defeated in 1999.

1139
01:45:35,500 --> 01:45:38,416
We killed more than
1,000 Pakistani soldiers.

1140
01:45:39,375 --> 01:45:43,375
That's when ISI provided me with
the most important intel of my life.

1141
01:45:43,750 --> 01:45:47,625
An Indian scientist was developing
a program for the Special Forces.

1142
01:45:48,625 --> 01:45:49,500
Alpha!

1143
01:45:52,583 --> 01:45:55,833
{\an8}<i>I met him, made friends with him.</i>

1144
01:45:57,458 --> 01:46:00,458
{\an8}If a war hero like you backs the program,

1145
01:46:00,541 --> 01:46:02,708
then Special Forces will take it forward.

1146
01:46:03,166 --> 01:46:04,791
{\an8}I'll get you the trial permission.

1147
01:46:06,458 --> 01:46:10,125
<i>And when the time was right,</i>
<i>I used you too, Guru </i>ji.

1148
01:46:10,833 --> 01:46:11,708
My Guru<i> ji.</i>

1149
01:46:11,791 --> 01:46:12,833
<i>They're bloody good.</i>

1150
01:46:13,000 --> 01:46:14,166
<i>And that's an understatement.</i>

1151
01:46:16,458 --> 01:46:17,750
ISI knew

1152
01:46:18,041 --> 01:46:19,916
if India successfully
created the Alpha serum,

1153
01:46:20,000 --> 01:46:22,208
then their army could never be defeated.

1154
01:46:23,583 --> 01:46:25,666
And that became my important mission.

1155
01:46:26,166 --> 01:46:28,625
To take the Alpha serum to Pakistan
at any cost.

1156
01:46:30,208 --> 01:46:33,416
But my obsession made me hasty.

1157
01:46:33,791 --> 01:46:35,583
<i>Alpha should have been tested</i>
<i>for another six months.</i>

1158
01:46:35,791 --> 01:46:36,958
<i>But you still pushed it.</i>

1159
01:46:37,041 --> 01:46:39,125
It has been shut down permanently.

1160
01:46:41,250 --> 01:46:42,333
<i>Jai Hind!</i>

1161
01:46:44,291 --> 01:46:45,791
I couldn't just give up.

1162
01:46:45,875 --> 01:46:47,625
I need money and men.

1163
01:46:48,000 --> 01:46:49,000
We trust you.

1164
01:46:50,000 --> 01:46:51,375
You'll have both.

1165
01:46:51,666 --> 01:46:53,083
<i>But how will you do it?</i>

1166
01:46:56,125 --> 01:46:58,458
Sita, you were the ace in my pack.

1167
01:46:58,541 --> 01:47:00,500
All your missions were not for India…

1168
01:47:02,125 --> 01:47:03,083
but for me.

1169
01:47:03,833 --> 01:47:05,291
For Pakistan.

1170
01:47:09,708 --> 01:47:11,083
I'll kill myself,

1171
01:47:12,291 --> 01:47:14,875
but I won't let your dream of Alpha
come true.

1172
01:47:20,583 --> 01:47:22,041
You don't need to fulfill my dream.

1173
01:47:23,458 --> 01:47:24,791
She will.

1174
01:47:47,375 --> 01:47:50,458
Body cam. I was getting a direct feed.

1175
01:47:53,458 --> 01:47:55,750
<i>When I saw that girl fight</i>
<i>alongside you,</i>

1176
01:47:56,125 --> 01:47:57,250
my head went into a spin.

1177
01:47:58,208 --> 01:47:59,333
I followed you.

1178
01:47:59,958 --> 01:48:02,000
<i>You left. Night fell.</i>

1179
01:48:02,750 --> 01:48:03,750
<i>That's when I found her.</i>

1180
01:48:13,083 --> 01:48:14,500
We three are soldiers,

1181
01:48:15,500 --> 01:48:17,791
but a war has only one winner.

1182
01:48:19,583 --> 01:48:21,583
Sita, I will pray for you,

1183
01:48:23,000 --> 01:48:24,583
but this is the cost of war.

1184
01:48:29,541 --> 01:48:32,333
And yes, it's not Fateh.

1185
01:48:34,666 --> 01:48:35,916
It's Major Zarrar Khan.

1186
01:48:39,208 --> 01:48:42,291
68th Falcon Regiment, Pakistan.

1187
01:49:04,083 --> 01:49:05,041
Sita.

1188
01:49:05,125 --> 01:49:07,083
- Exhaust fans!
- What?

1189
01:49:40,375 --> 01:49:41,375
Mine trap!

1190
01:49:46,333 --> 01:49:47,416
You need a counterweight.

1191
01:51:04,375 --> 01:51:05,458
What the hell is going on?

1192
01:51:06,166 --> 01:51:07,083
Bino.

1193
01:51:08,291 --> 01:51:12,583
Lt. Col. Fateh Singh Lakhawat
has sanctioned their entry, Captain.

1194
01:51:17,125 --> 01:51:20,416
What's all this medical equipment?
What's going on?

1195
01:51:20,916 --> 01:51:24,291
Sir, some men are carrying weapons too,
and they're not issued by Special Forces.

1196
01:51:26,375 --> 01:51:27,333
Come on, guys.

1197
01:51:34,000 --> 01:51:35,166
Where is Colonel Lakhawat?

1198
01:51:38,375 --> 01:51:39,583
Yes, Captain Rawat?

1199
01:51:40,750 --> 01:51:41,958
One question, sir.

1200
01:51:42,250 --> 01:51:43,166
Who are these people?

1201
01:51:43,541 --> 01:51:46,708
They don't look like our soldiers,
but they're still armed.

1202
01:51:47,791 --> 01:51:50,166
Are you questioning my authority,
Captain?

1203
01:51:51,416 --> 01:51:52,791
You're our senior, sir.

1204
01:51:53,291 --> 01:51:55,750
Following your orders is our duty.

1205
01:51:59,041 --> 01:52:00,541
{\an8}But above all, our loyalty

1206
01:52:01,916 --> 01:52:02,833
{\an8}lies with our country.

1207
01:52:15,916 --> 01:52:18,500
Well, then you leave me with no choice.

1208
01:52:18,916 --> 01:52:19,833
Surround them.

1209
01:52:23,500 --> 01:52:24,375
Keep moving.

1210
01:52:41,583 --> 01:52:45,250
<i>The Cherrapunji Special Forces base</i>
<i>is now under our control.</i>

1211
01:52:45,333 --> 01:52:46,291
<i>Congratulations!</i>

1212
01:52:46,375 --> 01:52:49,333
<i>We never thought Operation Odyssey</i>
<i>would succeed.</i>

1213
01:52:49,416 --> 01:52:50,500
But you made it!

1214
01:52:51,458 --> 01:52:54,458
<i>Our team is ready to extract you</i>
<i>at the Myanmar border.</i>

1215
01:52:54,875 --> 01:52:56,666
I must extract Alpha first.

1216
01:52:57,500 --> 01:52:59,333
Only then will I come home.

1217
01:53:00,416 --> 01:53:02,458
The preparation for the procedure
has started.

1218
01:53:04,208 --> 01:53:05,458
<i>I know what I'm doing.</i>

1219
01:53:06,666 --> 01:53:08,500
I've seen Sita fight.

1220
01:53:09,666 --> 01:53:13,166
When we have a thousand soldiers like her,

1221
01:53:13,791 --> 01:53:15,666
what do you think the outcome
of that war will be?

1222
01:53:16,500 --> 01:53:17,875
Victory will be ours.

1223
01:53:31,875 --> 01:53:33,958
I want the operation done ASAP.

1224
01:53:35,416 --> 01:53:36,875
We've just gotten a blood sample.

1225
01:53:36,958 --> 01:53:38,833
The results should take a few hours
to process.

1226
01:53:39,250 --> 01:53:40,958
In the meantime, let me set up
the operation theater.

1227
01:53:58,291 --> 01:53:59,458
You must know that…

1228
01:54:01,833 --> 01:54:06,625
any demon who harmed Sita
and Durga, even in the slightest,

1229
01:54:07,416 --> 01:54:08,958
died a horrifying death.

1230
01:54:12,291 --> 01:54:14,375
And here you are,
challenging both of them?

1231
01:54:17,708 --> 01:54:20,041
I cannot challenge Sita now.

1232
01:54:22,500 --> 01:54:23,625
She won't be coming.

1233
01:54:28,500 --> 01:54:29,666
Neither will Kaul.

1234
01:54:33,291 --> 01:54:34,958
Their chapter is closed.

1235
01:54:36,375 --> 01:54:38,750
Now, there's only you and me.

1236
01:54:55,291 --> 01:54:58,208
If there's an investigation, they'll
only find Sita and Kaul's dead bodies.

1237
01:54:58,750 --> 01:54:59,916
Everything else is clear.

1238
01:55:00,583 --> 01:55:02,166
I've reached the Srinagar airbase.

1239
01:55:02,458 --> 01:55:04,541
<i>Copy. I'll inform Major Zarrar.</i>

1240
01:55:11,958 --> 01:55:12,916
Let's go.

1241
01:56:01,958 --> 01:56:02,958
Where is he?

1242
01:56:20,500 --> 01:56:22,166
Cheetah X24, we see you.

1243
01:56:22,666 --> 01:56:23,750
Landing codes, please.

1244
01:56:24,416 --> 01:56:27,291
<i>Cheetah X24, we see you.</i>
<i>Landing codes, please.</i>

1245
01:56:28,125 --> 01:56:30,000
436522.

1246
01:56:30,375 --> 01:56:33,083
<i>I repeat, 436522.</i>

1247
01:56:35,541 --> 01:56:36,875
Give them landing permission.

1248
01:56:39,375 --> 01:56:40,625
Landing permission granted.

1249
01:56:57,333 --> 01:56:59,041
That wasn't the landing code!
It was the enemy code!

1250
01:57:09,250 --> 01:57:10,291
Jump as soon as we hit the tree line.

1251
01:57:26,666 --> 01:57:28,208
Send two teams to the forest.

1252
01:57:28,666 --> 01:57:30,833
This time, I want to see their corpses.

1253
01:57:32,958 --> 01:57:33,958
<i>Go! Go! Go!</i>

1254
01:57:35,083 --> 01:57:36,333
<i>Secure the exits!</i>

1255
01:57:38,916 --> 01:57:41,250
- Get ready. We're bringing her in.
- Yes, sir.

1256
01:57:56,125 --> 01:57:58,041
<i>Sir, the first jeep is coming back.</i>

1257
01:58:05,125 --> 01:58:06,041
Move! Move! Move!

1258
01:58:07,666 --> 01:58:09,208
Shoot the driver!

1259
01:58:22,833 --> 01:58:24,125
All units, fall back!

1260
01:59:30,000 --> 01:59:31,458
<i>Keep moving! Keep moving!</i>

1261
01:59:45,083 --> 01:59:47,208
<i>They have no ammunition left!</i>
<i>Keep moving!</i>

1262
01:59:48,541 --> 01:59:49,833
<i>Enter from the east side.</i>

1263
02:00:10,500 --> 02:00:11,875
<i>Glory to our nation!</i>

1264
02:00:15,083 --> 02:00:17,416
<i>Glory to Mother India!</i>

1265
02:00:59,750 --> 02:01:02,125
Pa, you're losing too much blood.

1266
02:01:04,375 --> 02:01:05,916
Sita, go.

1267
02:01:08,833 --> 02:01:09,916
Let's go, Pa!

1268
02:02:20,583 --> 02:02:22,583
You were a Pakistani soldier!

1269
02:02:26,250 --> 02:02:27,791
I used to call you "Baba."

1270
02:02:29,083 --> 02:02:30,541
This is war, Sita.

1271
02:02:31,458 --> 02:02:35,291
Which rule of war gave you the right

1272
02:02:35,916 --> 02:02:37,750
to snatch my childhood from me?

1273
02:02:38,708 --> 02:02:40,375
Wars have no rules,

1274
02:02:41,666 --> 02:02:43,291
but they come at a price.

1275
02:02:44,125 --> 02:02:45,875
A child paid that price,

1276
02:02:48,916 --> 02:02:51,208
but today, a soldier will take
revenge from you.

1277
02:02:52,458 --> 02:02:54,291
You cannot defeat me.

1278
02:02:56,000 --> 02:02:57,750
I have taught you everything.

1279
02:03:02,541 --> 02:03:04,833
And that will be your biggest mistake.

1280
02:03:10,208 --> 02:03:11,708
Today, I am not your Alpha.

1281
02:03:13,250 --> 02:03:14,458
I am India's Alpha!

1282
02:04:50,333 --> 02:04:51,750
You've become weak.

1283
02:05:13,500 --> 02:05:16,333
We'll kill these Indian soldiers
with their own tanks.

1284
02:05:21,583 --> 02:05:22,958
{\an8}Sir, the target is to your left.

1285
02:08:33,125 --> 02:08:34,083
Fateh.

1286
02:08:42,833 --> 02:08:44,833
People like you have only one end.

1287
02:08:50,750 --> 02:08:52,750
You cannot kill me, Kaul.

1288
02:08:56,750 --> 02:08:59,166
I'm not an ordinary soldier
like the others.

1289
02:09:00,000 --> 02:09:03,041
What happens to me will not
be decided by you,

1290
02:09:03,958 --> 02:09:07,208
but by people who have way more
authority than you.

1291
02:09:11,083 --> 02:09:12,166
Pakistan…

1292
02:09:13,375 --> 02:09:15,958
will never admit that
I am their spy.

1293
02:09:19,041 --> 02:09:20,083
And India…

1294
02:09:20,958 --> 02:09:23,125
will not be able to break me.

1295
02:09:24,208 --> 02:09:28,083
You'll get exhausted
torturing me in jail.

1296
02:09:32,541 --> 02:09:33,500
So you…

1297
02:09:34,625 --> 02:09:36,583
follow your protocol

1298
02:09:39,041 --> 02:09:41,041
and arrest me.

1299
02:09:49,458 --> 02:09:50,541
You are right.

1300
02:09:52,458 --> 02:09:55,708
If I kill you, I'll be answerable to many.

1301
02:10:00,666 --> 02:10:01,583
But she won't be.

1302
02:10:21,166 --> 02:10:22,666
For your family.

1303
02:10:30,250 --> 02:10:31,416
For yourself.

1304
02:10:41,916 --> 02:10:43,250
For India.

1305
02:10:46,791 --> 02:10:48,500
I want to be India's best soldier.

1306
02:10:57,041 --> 02:10:59,041
There's only one punishment
for a traitor.

1307
02:11:01,333 --> 02:11:02,208
Baba.

1308
02:12:33,291 --> 02:12:35,333
This was Janaki's favorite place.

1309
02:12:35,916 --> 02:12:36,791
Beautiful, isn't it?

1310
02:12:39,666 --> 02:12:41,458
You two are just like your mother.

1311
02:12:42,500 --> 02:12:45,958
Stubborn girls who can change the world.

1312
02:12:50,791 --> 02:12:52,208
I want both of you to disappear.

1313
02:12:53,666 --> 02:12:55,416
Durga, you have a life in Spain.

1314
02:12:56,041 --> 02:12:56,916
Go back there.

1315
02:12:57,541 --> 02:12:58,416
And Sita,

1316
02:12:59,458 --> 02:13:00,750
the life that was taken from you…

1317
02:13:02,041 --> 02:13:04,083
here's your chance to rebuild it.

1318
02:13:06,958 --> 02:13:08,250
That's what I want for both of you…

1319
02:13:09,791 --> 02:13:10,791
as your dad.

1320
02:13:12,833 --> 02:13:14,583
But I'm not just your dad.

1321
02:13:16,583 --> 02:13:18,250
I'm also RandAW Chief Vikrant Kaul.

1322
02:13:20,833 --> 02:13:23,375
That's why I have a job offer
for both of you.

1323
02:13:27,250 --> 02:13:28,291
Join me and my team?

1324
02:13:29,958 --> 02:13:31,625
Tiger, Pathaan, Kabir.

1325
02:13:33,166 --> 02:13:35,125
And with the best boss in the world…

1326
02:13:36,208 --> 02:13:37,125
India.

1327
02:17:07,916 --> 02:17:09,750
{\an8}This is the big girls' club.

1328
02:17:10,250 --> 02:17:11,333
{\an8}If you wanna play…

1329
02:17:12,291 --> 02:17:13,541
{\an8}Fall in line, little boy.

1330
02:17:13,916 --> 02:17:15,666
{\an8}'Cause you can't run away.

1331
02:17:16,500 --> 02:17:17,625
{\an8}There's nowhere to hide.

1332
02:17:17,708 --> 02:17:19,000
{\an8}There's nowhere to go.

1333
02:17:19,416 --> 02:17:22,375
{\an8}I've shattered the ceiling,
there's blood on the floor.

1334
02:17:23,125 --> 02:17:26,166
{\an8}A fight to the finish,
or a kiss goodbye.

1335
02:17:26,250 --> 02:17:29,000
{\an8}Get your last wish, baby,
'cause you're gonna die.